window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b036-dc6650bc65d1a0c6.json"]={sha256:"dc6650bc65d1a0c6df1b0e60fb93e0065646cbfe9b1f869315be8b237d931897",value:{"id":"b036","title":"懸索橋主纜架設","titleEn":"Suspension-bridge main-cable erection","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"主纜是懸索橋唯一幾乎無法更換的主構件，它的品質在架設時就已決定。本課比較空中紡線（金門大橋、大貝爾特東橋）與預製平行鋼絲索股（明石海峽大橋、瀨戶大橋、1915 恰納卡萊大橋）兩種工法，計算裸纜懸鏈線、索鞍彎曲應力、貓道張力與擠壓後直徑，說明鋼絲等級與鍍層、索股量測與統計允收，並依美國聯邦公路總署的指引談開纜檢查、腐蝕分級與剩餘強度評估。","summaryEn":"The main cable is the one primary member of a suspension bridge that can almost never be replaced, and its quality is fixed during erection. This course compares aerial spinning (Golden Gate, Great Belt East) with prefabricated parallel-wire strands (Akashi Kaikyo, Seto Ohashi, 1915 Çanakkale), computes bare-cable catenaries, saddle bending stress, catwalk tension and compacted diameter, explains wire grades and coatings, strand survey and statistical acceptance, and, following US Federal Highway Administration guidance, covers cable openings, corrosion staging and remaining-strength evaluation.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-suspension","subcategoryTitle":"懸索橋巨作與主纜系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Suspension bridges and main-cable systems","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-suspension","learningTags":["structures","st-suspension","cable"],"architectureFamily":"cable","architectureNodes":[["鋼絲與索股製造","Wire and strand manufacture"],["導索、貓道與牽引","Pilot rope, catwalk and hauling"],["索鞍、分束鞍與錨固","Saddles, splay and anchorage"],["擠壓、纏絲與索夾","Compaction, wrapping and bands"],["量測與允收","Survey and acceptance"],["開纜檢查與強度評估","Cable inspection and strength evaluation"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[4,1],[4,3],[3,5]],"diagram":{"type":"cable","labels":["鋼絲與索股製造","導索、貓道與牽引","索鞍、分束鞍與錨固","擠壓、纏絲與索夾","量測與允收"],"labelsEn":["Wire and strand manufacture","Pilot rope, catwalk and hauling","Saddles, splay and anchorage","Compaction, wrapping and bands","Survey and acceptance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：比較兩種工法完成同一條主纜的現場作業量。主纜需 36,000 根直徑 5.4 mm 的鋼絲，鋼絲面積 36,000×22.90 mm² ≈ 824,000 mm²，以 1,770 N/mm² 計破斷力 ≈ 1,459 MN。PWS 方案每股 127 根，需 284 股（最後一股不足 127 根時仍要一個完整錨頭），兩端共 568 個錨頭；若每夜牽引 4 股，約需 71 夜。空中紡線方案每束約 500 根，需 72 束、144 個索靴；若每日可鋪 1,600 根全長鋼絲，約需 36,000/1,600 ≈ 23 個有效工作日，但若可作業日比例只有 60%，實際約需 38 日曆天，並需加上每束垂度調整。擠壓後空隙率 20% 時主纜直徑 ≈ √(4×0.824/(π×0.80)) ≈ 1.15 m。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際橋梁的施工紀錄。","textEn":"Design exercise: compare site effort for the two methods on the same cable. The cable needs 36,000 wires of 5.4 mm, a steel area of 36,000×22.90 mm² ≈ 824,000 mm² and, at 1,770 N/mm², a breaking force ≈ 1,459 MN. The PWS option with 127 wires per strand needs 284 strands (the last, though short of 127 wires, still needs a full socket), 568 sockets at the two ends; at 4 strands a night it takes about 71 nights. The aerial-spinning option with about 500 wires per bundle needs 72 bundles and 144 strand shoes; laying 1,600 full-length wires a day takes about 36,000/1,600 ≈ 23 working days, but if only 60% of days are workable it takes about 38 calendar days, plus sag adjustment for each bundle. With 20% voids after compaction the cable diameter is ≈ √(4×0.824/(π×0.80)) ≈ 1.15 m. Values are teaching assumptions, not construction records of any real bridge.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b036-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「主纜架設工法的選擇」與「裸纜幾何：懸鏈線與拋物線」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Choosing the cable erection method\" and \"Bare-cable geometry: catenary versus parabola\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b036-v13-01","title":"主纜架設工法的選擇：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Choosing the cable erection method: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「空中紡線與預製索股」如何影響懸索橋主纜架設的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Aerial spinning versus PWS” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-bridge main-cable erection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"空中紡線法讓紡線輪沿貓道上方往返，每趟帶著鋼絲環從一座錨碇走到另一座，在現場把數百根鋼絲累積成一束：金門大橋每纜 61 束、平均每束約 452 根；大貝爾特東橋每纜 18,648 根鋼絲分成 37 束。預製平行鋼絲索股（PWS）則在工廠把鋼絲排成六角形索股並預裝錨頭，再整股牽引過海峽：明石海峽大橋每纜 290 股、瀨戶大橋與 1915 恰納卡萊大橋每股都是 127 根。空中紡線運輸輕便、錨固點少，但現場時間長且受風影響；PWS 現場快、品質在工廠控制，但索股重、錨頭多，需要大型捲盤與牽引設備。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「空中紡線與預製索股」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Aerial spinning runs spinning wheels back and forth above the catwalk, each trip carrying a loop of wire from one anchorage to the other, building bundles of several hundred wires on site: Golden Gate has 61 strands per cable averaging about 452 wires, and the Great Belt East Bridge splits 18,648 wires per cable into 37 bundles. Prefabricated parallel-wire strands (PWS) are laid up in the factory into hexagonal strands with sockets already fitted, then hauled across whole: Akashi Kaikyo has 290 strands per cable, and Seto Ohashi and the 1915 Çanakkale Bridge both use 127 wires per strand. Aerial spinning needs only light transport and few anchorage points but long, wind-sensitive site work; PWS is fast on site with factory-controlled quality but has heavy strands and many sockets, needing large reels and hauling gear. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Aerial spinning versus PWS” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：設主纜需 36,000 根鋼絲。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Suppose a cable needs 36,000 wires.","failure":"常見誤解：「預製索股一定比空中紡線先進，任何橋都應該使用。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Prefabricated strands are always more advanced and should be used on every bridge.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「空中紡線與預製索股」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Aerial spinning versus PWS”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-01-k1","title":"主纜架設工法的選擇","titleEn":"Choosing the cable erection method","text":"空中紡線法讓紡線輪沿貓道上方往返，每趟帶著鋼絲環從一座錨碇走到另一座，在現場把數百根鋼絲累積成一束：金門大橋每纜 61 束、平均每束約 452 根；大貝爾特東橋每纜 18,648 根鋼絲分成 37 束。預製平行鋼絲索股（PWS）則在工廠把鋼絲排成六角形索股並預裝錨頭，再整股牽引過海峽：明石海峽大橋每纜 290 股、瀨戶大橋與 1915 恰納卡萊大橋每股都是 127 根。","textEn":"Aerial spinning runs spinning wheels back and forth above the catwalk, each trip carrying a loop of wire from one anchorage to the other, building bundles of several hundred wires on site: Golden Gate has 61 strands per cable averaging about 452 wires, and the Great Belt East Bridge splits 18,648 wires per cable into 37 bundles. Prefabricated parallel-wire strands (PWS) are laid up in the factory into hexagonal strands with sockets already fitted, then hauled across whole: Akashi Kaikyo has 290 strands per cable, and Seto Ohashi and the 1915 Çanakkale Bridge both use 127 wires per strand.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：預製索股一定比空中紡線先進，任何橋都應該使用。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Prefabricated strands are always more advanced and should be used on every bridge. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「主纜架設工法的選擇」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Choosing the cable erection method\" is correct?","options":["預製索股一定比空中紡線先進，任何橋都應該使用。","空中紡線法讓紡線輪沿貓道上方往返，每趟帶著鋼絲環從一座錨碇走到另一座，在現場把數百根鋼絲累積成一束：金門大橋每纜 61 束、平均每束約 452 根。","主纜在任何階段都是拋物線，差別可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Prefabricated strands are always more advanced and should be used on every bridge.","Aerial spinning runs spinning wheels back and forth above the catwalk, each trip carrying a loop of wire from one anchorage to the other, building bundles of several hundred wires on site: Golden Gate has 61 strands per cable averaging about 452 wires, and the Great Belt East Bridge splits 18,648 wires per cable into 37 bundles.","The cable is a parabola at every stage, and the difference is negligible."],"answer":1,"explanation":"空中紡線法讓紡線輪沿貓道上方往返，每趟帶著鋼絲環從一座錨碇走到另一座，在現場把數百根鋼絲累積成一束：金門大橋每纜 61 束、平均每束約 452 根；大貝爾特東橋每纜 18,648 根鋼絲分成 37 束。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Aerial spinning runs spinning wheels back and forth above the catwalk, each trip carrying a loop of wire from one anchorage to the other, building bundles of several hundred wires on site: Golden Gate has 61 strands per cable averaging about 452 wires, and the Great Belt East Bridge splits 18,648 wires per cable into 37 bundles. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b036-v13-02","title":"主纜架設工法的選擇：定量估算","titleEn":"Choosing the cable erection method: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「空中紡線與預製索股」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Aerial spinning versus PWS” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：設主纜需 36,000 根鋼絲。PWS 每股 127 根需 36,000/127 ≈ 284 股、兩端共 568 個錨頭；空中紡線每束約 500 根只需 72 束、144 個索靴。若紡線輪每趟鋪 4 根鋼絲，空中紡線需約 36,000/4 = 9,000 趟，而 PWS 只需 284 次牽引。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Suppose a cable needs 36,000 wires. PWS with 127 per strand needs 36,000/127 ≈ 284 strands and 568 sockets at the two ends; aerial spinning with about 500 per bundle needs only 72 bundles and 144 strand shoes. If each wheel trip lays 4 wires, spinning needs about 36,000/4 = 9,000 trips, against 284 hauls for PWS. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以工期、氣象紀錄（可作業風速天數）、航道限制、運輸路線承重、錨碇空間與錨頭數量做工法比選矩陣，並估算每種工法的現場人時與風險；選定後由設計者確認錨碇與索鞍細部符合所選工法。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build a comparison matrix of programme, weather records (days with workable wind), navigation limits, transport-route capacity, anchorage space and socket count, estimating site man-hours and risk for each method; once chosen, the designer confirms that anchorage and saddle details suit the method.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"設主纜需 36,000 根鋼絲。PWS 每股 127 根需 36,000/127 ≈ 284 股、兩端共 568 個錨頭；空中紡線每束約 500 根只需 72 束、144 個索靴。若紡線輪每趟鋪 4 根鋼絲，空中紡線需約 36,000/4 = 9,000 趟，而 PWS 只需 284 次牽引。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Suppose a cable needs 36,000 wires. PWS with 127 per strand needs 36,000/127 ≈ 284 strands and 568 sockets at the two ends; aerial spinning with about 500 per bundle needs only 72 bundles and 144 strand shoes. If each wheel trip lays 4 wires, spinning needs about 36,000/4 = 9,000 trips, against 284 hauls for PWS. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「主纜架設工法的選擇」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Choosing the cable erection method\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼絲只承受軸向拉力，索鞍形狀不影響應力。","主纜擠壓只是為了外觀圓整，對耐久性影響不大。","設主纜需 36,000 根鋼絲。"],"optionsEn":["Cable wires carry only axial tension, so saddle shape does not affect stress.","Compaction is only to make the cable look round and hardly affects durability.","Suppose a cable needs 36,000 wires."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設主纜需 36,000 根鋼絲。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Suppose a cable needs 36,000 wires. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b036-v13-03","title":"主纜架設工法的選擇：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Choosing the cable erection method: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「空中紡線與預製索股」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Aerial spinning versus PWS” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以工期、氣象紀錄（可作業風速天數）、航道限制、運輸路線承重、錨碇空間與錨頭數量做工法比選矩陣，並估算每種工法的現場人時與風險；選定後由設計者確認錨碇與索鞍細部符合所選工法。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build a comparison matrix of programme, weather records (days with workable wind), navigation limits, transport-route capacity, anchorage space and socket count, estimating site man-hours and risk for each method; once chosen, the designer confirms that anchorage and saddle details suit the method. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：工法比選應在基本設計階段完成，並把結果寫入錨碇、索鞍與貓道的設計條件；投標文件可允許替代工法，但必須要求承包商提出相應的錨固與幾何控制方案，並經設計者核可。","observationEn":"Site practice: Settle the method comparison at basic design and write the outcome into the design conditions for anchorages, saddles and catwalks; tender documents may allow alternatives, but the contractor must then submit matching anchorage and geometry-control proposals for the designer's approval.","failure":"注意干擾：在強風頻繁的海峽採用空中紡線而未預留停工天數，進度落後時容易壓縮垂度調整時間；採用 PWS 卻低估捲盤重量與運輸限制，可能必須縮短索股長度或增加接頭，影響錨固設計。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Choosing aerial spinning over a windy strait without allowing for downtime tempts crews to cut sag adjustment when behind; choosing PWS while underestimating reel weight and transport limits may force shorter strands or extra splices that affect anchorage design. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以工期、氣象紀錄（可作業風速天數）、航道限制、運輸路線承重、錨碇空間與錨頭數量做工法比選矩陣，並估算每種工法的現場人時與風險；選定後由設計者確認錨碇與索鞍細部符合所選工法。","textEn":"Build a comparison matrix of programme, weather records (days with workable wind), navigation limits, transport-route capacity, anchorage space and socket count, estimating site man-hours and risk for each method; once chosen, the designer confirms that anchorage and saddle details suit the method.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"工法比選應在基本設計階段完成，並把結果寫入錨碇、索鞍與貓道的設計條件；投標文件可允許替代工法，但必須要求承包商提出相應的錨固與幾何控制方案，並經設計者核可。","textEn":"Settle the method comparison at basic design and write the outcome into the design conditions for anchorages, saddles and catwalks; tender documents may allow alternatives, but the contractor must then submit matching anchorage and geometry-control proposals for the designer's approval.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「主纜架設工法的選擇」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Choosing the cable erection method\"?","options":["以工期、氣象紀錄（可作業風速天數）、航道限制、運輸路線承重、錨碇空間與錨頭數量做工法比選矩陣，並估算每種工法的現場人時與風險。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要平均強度高於規格，整批鋼絲就合格。"],"optionsEn":["Build a comparison matrix of programme, weather records (days with workable wind), navigation limits, transport-route capacity, anchorage space and socket count, estimating site man-hours and risk for each method.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If the mean strength is above specification, the whole lot passes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以工期、氣象紀錄（可作業風速天數）、航道限制、運輸路線承重、錨碇空間與錨頭數量做工法比選矩陣，並估算每種工法的現場人時與風險；選定後由設計者確認錨碇與索鞍細部符合所選工法。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build a comparison matrix of programme, weather records (days with workable wind), navigation limits, transport-route capacity, anchorage space and socket count, estimating site man-hours and risk for each method; once chosen, the designer confirms that anchorage and saddle details suit the method. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b036-v13-04","title":"主纜架設工法的選擇：失效診斷","titleEn":"Choosing the cable erection method: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「空中紡線與預製索股」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Aerial spinning versus PWS” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"在強風頻繁的海峽採用空中紡線而未預留停工天數，進度落後時容易壓縮垂度調整時間；採用 PWS 卻低估捲盤重量與運輸限制，可能必須縮短索股長度或增加接頭，影響錨固設計。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Choosing aerial spinning over a windy strait without allowing for downtime tempts crews to cut sag adjustment when behind; choosing PWS while underestimating reel weight and transport limits may force shorter strands or extra splices that affect anchorage design. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：空中紡線運輸輕便、錨固點少，但現場時間長且受風影響；PWS 現場快、品質在工廠控制，但索股重、錨頭多，需要大型捲盤與牽引設備。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Aerial spinning needs only light transport and few anchorage points but long, wind-sensitive site work; PWS is fast on site with factory-controlled quality but has heavy strands and many sockets, needing large reels and hauling gear.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「預製索股一定比空中紡線先進，任何橋都應該使用。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Prefabricated strands are always more advanced and should be used on every bridge.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在強風頻繁的海峽採用空中紡線而未預留停工天數，進度落後時容易壓縮垂度調整時間；採用 PWS 卻低估捲盤重量與運輸限制，可能必須縮短索股長度或增加接頭，影響錨固設計。","textEn":"Choosing aerial spinning over a windy strait without allowing for downtime tempts crews to cut sag adjustment when behind; choosing PWS while underestimating reel weight and transport limits may force shorter strands or extra splices that affect anchorage design.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「主纜架設工法的選擇」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Choosing the cable erection method\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","在強風頻繁的海峽採用空中紡線而未預留停工天數，進度落後時容易壓縮垂度調整時間。","主纜在任何階段都是拋物線，差別可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Choosing aerial spinning over a windy strait without allowing for downtime tempts crews to cut sag adjustment when behind.","The cable is a parabola at every stage, and the difference is negligible."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在強風頻繁的海峽採用空中紡線而未預留停工天數，進度落後時容易壓縮垂度調整時間；採用 PWS 卻低估捲盤重量與運輸限制，可能必須縮短索股長度或增加接頭，影響錨固設計。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Choosing aerial spinning over a windy strait without allowing for downtime tempts crews to cut sag adjustment when behind; choosing PWS while underestimating reel weight and transport limits may force shorter strands or extra splices that affect anchorage design. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b036-v13-05","title":"裸纜幾何：懸鏈線與拋物線：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Bare-cable geometry: catenary versus parabola: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「裸纜懸鏈線」如何影響懸索橋主纜架設的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bare-cable catenary” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-bridge main-cable erection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主纜在橋面掛上之前只承受自重，自重沿纜長均勻分布，形狀是懸鏈線；掛上沿水平均勻分布的橋面後，形狀才接近拋物線。設計者先決定完工狀態的線形，再以逆向分析扣除橋面荷重與彈性伸長，求出主纜在無應力狀態下的長度，以及裸纜階段各跨應有的垂度與索鞍位置。架設時第一根基準索股或基準鋼絲就是按這個裸纜幾何設定，之後所有鋼絲都以它為準，因此裸纜計算的誤差會一路傳到完工線形。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「裸纜懸鏈線」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Before the deck is hung, the main cable carries only its own weight, distributed evenly along its length, so its shape is a catenary; once a deck load distributed evenly along the horizontal is added, the shape approaches a parabola. Designers fix the completed profile first, then back-analyse by removing deck load and elastic stretch to find the unstressed cable length and the bare-cable sag and saddle positions for each span. The first reference strand or reference wire is set to this bare-cable geometry and every later wire follows it, so errors in the bare-cable calculation pass straight into the final profile. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Bare-cable catenary” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：取裸纜自重 w = 35 kN/m、水平張力 H = 70,000 kN、跨徑 l = 1,600 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Take bare-cable weight w = 35 kN/m, horizontal tension H = 70,000 kN and span l = 1,600 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「主纜在任何階段都是拋物線，差別可以忽略。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The cable is a parabola at every stage, and the difference is negligible.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「裸纜懸鏈線」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Bare-cable catenary”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-05-k1","title":"裸纜幾何：懸鏈線與拋物線","titleEn":"Bare-cable geometry: catenary versus parabola","text":"主纜在橋面掛上之前只承受自重，自重沿纜長均勻分布，形狀是懸鏈線；掛上沿水平均勻分布的橋面後，形狀才接近拋物線。設計者先決定完工狀態的線形，再以逆向分析扣除橋面荷重與彈性伸長，求出主纜在無應力狀態下的長度，以及裸纜階段各跨應有的垂度與索鞍位置。","textEn":"Before the deck is hung, the main cable carries only its own weight, distributed evenly along its length, so its shape is a catenary; once a deck load distributed evenly along the horizontal is added, the shape approaches a parabola. Designers fix the completed profile first, then back-analyse by removing deck load and elastic stretch to find the unstressed cable length and the bare-cable sag and saddle positions for each span.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：主纜在任何階段都是拋物線，差別可以忽略。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The cable is a parabola at every stage, and the difference is negligible. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「裸纜幾何：懸鏈線與拋物線」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bare-cable geometry: catenary versus parabola\" is correct?","options":["主纜在任何階段都是拋物線，差別可以忽略。","鍍鋅只是外觀處理，對主纜壽命影響不大。","主纜在橋面掛上之前只承受自重，自重沿纜長均勻分布，形狀是懸鏈線；掛上沿水平均勻分布的橋面後，形狀才接近拋物線。"],"optionsEn":["The cable is a parabola at every stage, and the difference is negligible.","Galvanising is cosmetic and hardly affects cable life.","Before the deck is hung, the main cable carries only its own weight, distributed evenly along its length, so its shape is a catenary."],"answer":2,"explanation":"主纜在橋面掛上之前只承受自重，自重沿纜長均勻分布，形狀是懸鏈線；掛上沿水平均勻分布的橋面後，形狀才接近拋物線。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Before the deck is hung, the main cable carries only its own weight, distributed evenly along its length, so its shape is a catenary; once a deck load distributed evenly along the horizontal is added, the shape approaches a parabola. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b036-v13-06","title":"裸纜幾何：懸鏈線與拋物線：定量估算","titleEn":"Bare-cable geometry: catenary versus parabola: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「裸纜懸鏈線」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bare-cable catenary” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：取裸纜自重 w = 35 kN/m、水平張力 H = 70,000 kN、跨徑 l = 1,600 m。拋物線 f_p = w·l²/(8H) = 35×1,600²/560,000 = 160.0 m；懸鏈線 f_c = (H/w)·[cosh(w·l/(2H)) − 1] = 2,000×(cosh 0.4 − 1) = 2,000×0.0811 ≈ 162.1 m，相差約 2.1 m（1.3%）。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Take bare-cable weight w = 35 kN/m, horizontal tension H = 70,000 kN and span l = 1,600 m. The parabola gives f_p = w·l²/(8H) = 35×1,600²/560,000 = 160.0 m; the catenary gives f_c = (H/w)·[cosh(w·l/(2H)) − 1] = 2,000×(cosh 0.4 − 1) = 2,000×0.0811 ≈ 162.1 m, a difference of about 2.1 m (1.3%). Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以兩套獨立程式（例如設計者與承包商各自的非線性分析）計算無應力纜長與裸纜垂度，比較結果；基準索股架設後量測各跨垂度與索鞍位置，經溫度修正後與計算值比較，差異超過允差時先複核計算假設再調整。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compute unstressed cable length and bare-cable sag with two independent programs, such as the designer's and the contractor's nonlinear analyses, and compare; after the reference strand is erected, measure sag in each span and saddle positions, correct for temperature and compare with calculation, re-checking assumptions before adjusting when differences exceed tolerance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"取裸纜自重 w = 35 kN/m、水平張力 H = 70,000 kN、跨徑 l = 1,600 m。拋物線 f_p = w·l²/(8H) = 35×1,600²/560,000 = 160.0 m；懸鏈線 f_c = (H/w)·[cosh(w·l/(2H)) − 1] = 2,000×(cosh 0.4 − 1) = 2,000×0.0811 ≈ 162.1 m，相差約 2.1 m（1.3%）。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Take bare-cable weight w = 35 kN/m, horizontal tension H = 70,000 kN and span l = 1,600 m. The parabola gives f_p = w·l²/(8H) = 35×1,600²/560,000 = 160.0 m; the catenary gives f_c = (H/w)·[cosh(w·l/(2H)) − 1] = 2,000×(cosh 0.4 − 1) = 2,000×0.0811 ≈ 162.1 m, a difference of about 2.1 m (1.3%). Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「裸纜幾何：懸鏈線與拋物線」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bare-cable geometry: catenary versus parabola\", which statement holds?","options":["取裸纜自重 w = 35 kN/m、水平張力 H = 70,000 kN、跨徑 l = 1,600 m。","貓道只是臨時走道，可以用一般鷹架的標準設計。","儀器越精密，就不需要相對量測與交叉核對。"],"optionsEn":["Take bare-cable weight w = 35 kN/m, horizontal tension H = 70,000 kN and span l = 1,600 m.","A catwalk is only a temporary walkway and can be designed like ordinary scaffolding.","With precise enough instruments, relative measurement and cross-checks are unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"取裸纜自重 w = 35 kN/m、水平張力 H = 70,000 kN、跨徑 l = 1,600 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Take bare-cable weight w = 35 kN/m, horizontal tension H = 70,000 kN and span l = 1,600 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b036-v13-07","title":"裸纜幾何：懸鏈線與拋物線：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bare-cable geometry: catenary versus parabola: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「裸纜懸鏈線」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bare-cable catenary” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以兩套獨立程式（例如設計者與承包商各自的非線性分析）計算無應力纜長與裸纜垂度，比較結果；基準索股架設後量測各跨垂度與索鞍位置，經溫度修正後與計算值比較，差異超過允差時先複核計算假設再調整。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compute unstressed cable length and bare-cable sag with two independent programs, such as the designer's and the contractor's nonlinear analyses, and compare; after the reference strand is erected, measure sag in each span and saddle positions, correct for temperature and compare with calculation, re-checking assumptions before adjusting when differences exceed tolerance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：架設手冊應列出裸纜階段的目標垂度、索鞍預偏量、參考溫度與量測點位置，並附上兩套獨立計算的比對結果；基準索股定位是全工程最重要的停留點之一，須由設計者與監造共同見證。","observationEn":"Site practice: The erection manual should list target bare-cable sags, saddle offsets, reference temperature and survey points, with the comparison of two independent calculations; setting the reference strand is one of the most important hold points of the whole job and must be witnessed jointly by the designer and the supervising engineer.","failure":"注意干擾：若裸纜階段直接用拋物線公式設定基準索股，在大跨中會產生公尺級的垂度誤差，完工後橋面高程與吊索長度都對不上；忽略索鞍與錨碇處的實際幾何（切點位置、分束長度）也會造成同樣的系統誤差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Setting the reference strand with the parabola formula in the bare-cable stage creates sag errors of the order of metres on a long span, so deck levels and hanger lengths do not match at completion; ignoring the real geometry at saddles and anchorages, such as tangent points and splay lengths, causes similar systematic errors. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以兩套獨立程式（例如設計者與承包商各自的非線性分析）計算無應力纜長與裸纜垂度，比較結果；基準索股架設後量測各跨垂度與索鞍位置，經溫度修正後與計算值比較，差異超過允差時先複核計算假設再調整。","textEn":"Compute unstressed cable length and bare-cable sag with two independent programs, such as the designer's and the contractor's nonlinear analyses, and compare; after the reference strand is erected, measure sag in each span and saddle positions, correct for temperature and compare with calculation, re-checking assumptions before adjusting when differences exceed tolerance.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"架設手冊應列出裸纜階段的目標垂度、索鞍預偏量、參考溫度與量測點位置，並附上兩套獨立計算的比對結果；基準索股定位是全工程最重要的停留點之一，須由設計者與監造共同見證。","textEn":"The erection manual should list target bare-cable sags, saddle offsets, reference temperature and survey points, with the comparison of two independent calculations; setting the reference strand is one of the most important hold points of the whole job and must be witnessed jointly by the designer and the supervising engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「裸纜幾何：懸鏈線與拋物線」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bare-cable geometry: catenary versus parabola\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以兩套獨立程式（例如設計者與承包商各自的非線性分析）計算無應力纜長與裸纜垂度，比較結果。","主纜外觀完好、塗裝沒有剝落，內部鋼絲就一定沒有腐蝕。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Compute unstressed cable length and bare-cable sag with two independent programs, such as the designer's and the contractor's nonlinear analyses, and compare.","If the cable looks sound and its paint is intact, the wires inside cannot be corroded."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以兩套獨立程式（例如設計者與承包商各自的非線性分析）計算無應力纜長與裸纜垂度，比較結果；基準索股架設後量測各跨垂度與索鞍位置，經溫度修正後與計算值比較，差異超過允差時先複核計算假設再調整。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compute unstressed cable length and bare-cable sag with two independent programs, such as the designer's and the contractor's nonlinear analyses, and compare; after the reference strand is erected, measure sag in each span and saddle positions, correct for temperature and compare with calculation, re-checking assumptions before adjusting when differences exceed tolerance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b036-v13-08","title":"裸纜幾何：懸鏈線與拋物線：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bare-cable geometry: catenary versus parabola: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「裸纜懸鏈線」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bare-cable catenary” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若裸纜階段直接用拋物線公式設定基準索股，在大跨中會產生公尺級的垂度誤差，完工後橋面高程與吊索長度都對不上；忽略索鞍與錨碇處的實際幾何（切點位置、分束長度）也會造成同樣的系統誤差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Setting the reference strand with the parabola formula in the bare-cable stage creates sag errors of the order of metres on a long span, so deck levels and hanger lengths do not match at completion; ignoring the real geometry at saddles and anchorages, such as tangent points and splay lengths, causes similar systematic errors. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：架設時第一根基準索股或基準鋼絲就是按這個裸纜幾何設定，之後所有鋼絲都以它為準，因此裸纜計算的誤差會一路傳到完工線形。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The first reference strand or reference wire is set to this bare-cable geometry and every later wire follows it, so errors in the bare-cable calculation pass straight into the final profile.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「主纜在任何階段都是拋物線，差別可以忽略。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The cable is a parabola at every stage, and the difference is negligible.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若裸纜階段直接用拋物線公式設定基準索股，在大跨中會產生公尺級的垂度誤差，完工後橋面高程與吊索長度都對不上；忽略索鞍與錨碇處的實際幾何（切點位置、分束長度）也會造成同樣的系統誤差。","textEn":"Setting the reference strand with the parabola formula in the bare-cable stage creates sag errors of the order of metres on a long span, so deck levels and hanger lengths do not match at completion; ignoring the real geometry at saddles and anchorages, such as tangent points and splay lengths, causes similar systematic errors.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「裸纜幾何：懸鏈線與拋物線」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bare-cable geometry: catenary versus parabola\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","鍍鋅只是外觀處理，對主纜壽命影響不大。","若裸纜階段直接用拋物線公式設定基準索股，在大跨中會產生公尺級的垂度誤差，完工後橋面高程與吊索長度都對不上。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Galvanising is cosmetic and hardly affects cable life.","Setting the reference strand with the parabola formula in the bare-cable stage creates sag errors of the order of metres on a long span, so deck levels and hanger lengths do not match at completion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若裸纜階段直接用拋物線公式設定基準索股，在大跨中會產生公尺級的垂度誤差，完工後橋面高程與吊索長度都對不上；忽略索鞍與錨碇處的實際幾何（切點位置、分束長度）也會造成同樣的系統誤差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Setting the reference strand with the parabola formula in the bare-cable stage creates sag errors of the order of metres on a long span, so deck levels and hanger lengths do not match at completion; ignoring the real geometry at saddles and anchorages, such as tangent points and splay lengths, causes similar systematic errors. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b036-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「主纜鋼絲的強度等級與鍍層」與「索鞍、分束與錨固細部」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Strength grades and coatings of cable wire\" and \"Saddles, splay and anchorage details\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b036-v13-09","title":"主纜鋼絲的強度等級與鍍層：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Strength grades and coatings of cable wire: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「鋼絲等級與鍍鋅層」如何影響懸索橋主纜架設的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wire grade and zinc coating” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-bridge main-cable erection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主纜鋼絲是經鉛浴或替代熱處理、冷拉成形的高碳鋼絲，再熱浸鍍鋅。日本製鐵的技術報告指出，日本約半世紀使用 1,570 MPa 級鋼絲，1,770 MPa 級 5 mm 鋼絲首次用於明石海峽大橋，近年已試製 1,960 MPa 級；長大橋鋼絲的鍍鋅量一般在 300 g/m² 以上，近年也採用鋅鋁合金鍍層。強度越高，所需鋼絲越少、自重越輕，但對缺口、氫脆與彎曲越敏感，扭轉與伸長率等延性指標必須同時控制。鍍層是犧牲性防蝕，架設時的刮傷會成為日後腐蝕的起點。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鋼絲等級與鍍鋅層」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cable wire is high-carbon steel, heat-treated by lead patenting or an alternative, cold-drawn and hot-dip galvanised. A Nippon Steel technical report notes that Japan used 1,570 MPa wire for about half a century, that 1,770 MPa 5 mm wire was first used on the Akashi Kaikyo Bridge, and that 1,960 MPa wire has since been trial-produced; long-span bridge wire usually carries 300 g/m² or more of zinc, with zinc–aluminium coatings used in recent years. Higher strength means fewer wires and less self-weight but more sensitivity to notches, hydrogen embrittlement and bending, so ductility indicators such as torsion and elongation must be controlled too. The coating is sacrificial, and scratches during erection become future corrosion sites. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Wire grade and zinc coating” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：金門大橋鋼絲鍍鋅厚度約 0.002 in = 50.8 μm，以鋅密度 7.14 g/cm³ 換算約 50.8×7.14 ≈ 363 g/m²，符合 300 g/m² 以上的常見水準。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Golden Gate wire carries about 0.002 in = 50.8 μm of zinc, which at a zinc density of 7.14 g/cm³ is about 50.8×7.14 ≈ 363 g/m², in line with the usual 300 g/m² or more.","failure":"常見誤解：「鍍鋅只是外觀處理，對主纜壽命影響不大。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Galvanising is cosmetic and hardly affects cable life.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鋼絲等級與鍍鋅層」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Wire grade and zinc coating”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-09-k1","title":"主纜鋼絲的強度等級與鍍層","titleEn":"Strength grades and coatings of cable wire","text":"主纜鋼絲是經鉛浴或替代熱處理、冷拉成形的高碳鋼絲，再熱浸鍍鋅。日本製鐵的技術報告指出，日本約半世紀使用 1,570 MPa 級鋼絲，1,770 MPa 級 5 mm 鋼絲首次用於明石海峽大橋，近年已試製 1,960 MPa 級；長大橋鋼絲的鍍鋅量一般在 300 g/m² 以上，近年也採用鋅鋁合金鍍層。","textEn":"Cable wire is high-carbon steel, heat-treated by lead patenting or an alternative, cold-drawn and hot-dip galvanised. A Nippon Steel technical report notes that Japan used 1,570 MPa wire for about half a century, that 1,770 MPa 5 mm wire was first used on the Akashi Kaikyo Bridge, and that 1,960 MPa wire has since been trial-produced; long-span bridge wire usually carries 300 g/m² or more of zinc, with zinc–aluminium coatings used in recent years.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鍍鋅只是外觀處理，對主纜壽命影響不大。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Galvanising is cosmetic and hardly affects cable life. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「主纜鋼絲的強度等級與鍍層」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Strength grades and coatings of cable wire\" is correct?","options":["主纜鋼絲是經鉛浴或替代熱處理、冷拉成形的高碳鋼絲，再熱浸鍍鋅。","鍍鋅只是外觀處理，對主纜壽命影響不大。","鋼絲只承受軸向拉力，索鞍形狀不影響應力。"],"optionsEn":["Cable wire is high-carbon steel, heat-treated by lead patenting or an alternative, cold-drawn and hot-dip galvanised.","Galvanising is cosmetic and hardly affects cable life.","Cable wires carry only axial tension, so saddle shape does not affect stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"主纜鋼絲是經鉛浴或替代熱處理、冷拉成形的高碳鋼絲，再熱浸鍍鋅。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cable wire is high-carbon steel, heat-treated by lead patenting or an alternative, cold-drawn and hot-dip galvanised. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b036-v13-10","title":"主纜鋼絲的強度等級與鍍層：定量估算","titleEn":"Strength grades and coatings of cable wire: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼絲等級與鍍鋅層」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wire grade and zinc coating” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：金門大橋鋼絲鍍鋅厚度約 0.002 in = 50.8 μm，以鋅密度 7.14 g/cm³ 換算約 50.8×7.14 ≈ 363 g/m²，符合 300 g/m² 以上的常見水準。若同一主纜由 1,570 MPa 改用 1,960 MPa 鋼絲而破斷力不變，鋼絲面積可減少 1 − 1,570/1,960 ≈ 20%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Golden Gate wire carries about 0.002 in = 50.8 μm of zinc, which at a zinc density of 7.14 g/cm³ is about 50.8×7.14 ≈ 363 g/m², in line with the usual 300 g/m² or more. Replacing 1,570 MPa wire with 1,960 MPa wire at the same breaking force cuts wire area by 1 − 1,570/1,960 ≈ 20%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每捲鋼絲抽驗直徑、抗拉強度、0.2% 耐力、伸長率、扭轉與捲繞試驗、鍍層附著量與附著性；架設前後在牽引路徑上的導輪、索鞍槽與擠壓機接觸面檢查刮傷，並抽樣量測鍍層厚度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample each coil for diameter, tensile strength, 0.2% proof stress, elongation, torsion and wrapping tests, coating mass and adhesion; before and after erection inspect rollers, saddle grooves and compactor contact surfaces along the hauling path for scratches, sampling coating thickness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"金門大橋鋼絲鍍鋅厚度約 0.002 in = 50.8 μm，以鋅密度 7.14 g/cm³ 換算約 50.8×7.14 ≈ 363 g/m²，符合 300 g/m² 以上的常見水準。若同一主纜由 1,570 MPa 改用 1,960 MPa 鋼絲而破斷力不變，鋼絲面積可減少 1 − 1,570/1,960 ≈ 20%。","textEn":"Golden Gate wire carries about 0.002 in = 50.8 μm of zinc, which at a zinc density of 7.14 g/cm³ is about 50.8×7.14 ≈ 363 g/m², in line with the usual 300 g/m² or more. Replacing 1,570 MPa wire with 1,960 MPa wire at the same breaking force cuts wire area by 1 − 1,570/1,960 ≈ 20%.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「主纜鋼絲的強度等級與鍍層」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Strength grades and coatings of cable wire\", which statement holds?","options":["主纜擠壓只是為了外觀圓整，對耐久性影響不大。","金門大橋鋼絲鍍鋅厚度約 0.002 in = 50.8 μm，以鋅密度 7.14 g/cm³ 換算約 50.8×7.14 ≈ 363 g/m²，符合 300 g/m² 以上的常見水準。","只要平均強度高於規格，整批鋼絲就合格。"],"optionsEn":["Compaction is only to make the cable look round and hardly affects durability.","Golden Gate wire carries about 0.002 in = 50.8 μm of zinc, which at a zinc density of 7.14 g/cm³ is about 50.8×7.14 ≈ 363 g/m², in line with the usual 300 g/m² or more.","If the mean strength is above specification, the whole lot passes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"金門大橋鋼絲鍍鋅厚度約 0.002 in = 50.8 μm，以鋅密度 7.14 g/cm³ 換算約 50.8×7.14 ≈ 363 g/m²，符合 300 g/m² 以上的常見水準。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Golden Gate wire carries about 0.002 in = 50.8 μm of zinc, which at a zinc density of 7.14 g/cm³ is about 50.8×7.14 ≈ 363 g/m², in line with the usual 300 g/m² or more. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b036-v13-11","title":"主纜鋼絲的強度等級與鍍層：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Strength grades and coatings of cable wire: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼絲等級與鍍鋅層」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wire grade and zinc coating” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每捲鋼絲抽驗直徑、抗拉強度、0.2% 耐力、伸長率、扭轉與捲繞試驗、鍍層附著量與附著性；架設前後在牽引路徑上的導輪、索鞍槽與擠壓機接觸面檢查刮傷，並抽樣量測鍍層厚度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample each coil for diameter, tensile strength, 0.2% proof stress, elongation, torsion and wrapping tests, coating mass and adhesion; before and after erection inspect rollers, saddle grooves and compactor contact surfaces along the hauling path for scratches, sampling coating thickness. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：鋼絲規格須同時訂定強度、延性與鍍層指標及抽樣頻率，並要求從線材爐號到成品捲號的完整追溯；牽引與擠壓設備的接觸面材料與狀態應列入每日檢查表。","observationEn":"Site practice: The wire specification must set strength, ductility and coating requirements with sampling frequencies and require full traceability from rod heat to finished coil; the material and condition of contact surfaces on hauling and compaction equipment belong on the daily checklist.","failure":"注意干擾：鍍鋅層在牽引或擠壓時被大面積刮除，日後在纜內潮濕環境中最先出現鏽點；超高強度鋼絲若延性不足，在索鞍或索夾附近的局部彎曲處可能脆斷，而且斷絲藏在纜內不易被發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Large areas of zinc scraped off during hauling or compaction are where rust first appears in a damp cable; ultra-high-strength wire with poor ductility can break brittly where it bends locally at saddles or bands, hidden inside the cable. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每捲鋼絲抽驗直徑、抗拉強度、0.2% 耐力、伸長率、扭轉與捲繞試驗、鍍層附著量與附著性；架設前後在牽引路徑上的導輪、索鞍槽與擠壓機接觸面檢查刮傷，並抽樣量測鍍層厚度。","textEn":"Sample each coil for diameter, tensile strength, 0.2% proof stress, elongation, torsion and wrapping tests, coating mass and adhesion; before and after erection inspect rollers, saddle grooves and compactor contact surfaces along the hauling path for scratches, sampling coating thickness.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"鋼絲規格須同時訂定強度、延性與鍍層指標及抽樣頻率，並要求從線材爐號到成品捲號的完整追溯；牽引與擠壓設備的接觸面材料與狀態應列入每日檢查表。","textEn":"The wire specification must set strength, ductility and coating requirements with sampling frequencies and require full traceability from rod heat to finished coil; the material and condition of contact surfaces on hauling and compaction equipment belong on the daily checklist.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「主纜鋼絲的強度等級與鍍層」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Strength grades and coatings of cable wire\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","主纜強度在完工時就確定，之後只需目視檢查外觀。","每捲鋼絲抽驗直徑、抗拉強度、0.2% 耐力、伸長率、扭轉與捲繞試驗、鍍層附著量與附著性。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Cable strength is fixed at completion, so only visual checks of the outside are needed afterwards.","Sample each coil for diameter, tensile strength, 0.2% proof stress, elongation, torsion and wrapping tests, coating mass and adhesion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每捲鋼絲抽驗直徑、抗拉強度、0.2% 耐力、伸長率、扭轉與捲繞試驗、鍍層附著量與附著性；架設前後在牽引路徑上的導輪、索鞍槽與擠壓機接觸面檢查刮傷，並抽樣量測鍍層厚度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample each coil for diameter, tensile strength, 0.2% proof stress, elongation, torsion and wrapping tests, coating mass and adhesion; before and after erection inspect rollers, saddle grooves and compactor contact surfaces along the hauling path for scratches, sampling coating thickness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b036-v13-12","title":"主纜鋼絲的強度等級與鍍層：失效診斷","titleEn":"Strength grades and coatings of cable wire: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼絲等級與鍍鋅層」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wire grade and zinc coating” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"鍍鋅層在牽引或擠壓時被大面積刮除，日後在纜內潮濕環境中最先出現鏽點；超高強度鋼絲若延性不足，在索鞍或索夾附近的局部彎曲處可能脆斷，而且斷絲藏在纜內不易被發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Large areas of zinc scraped off during hauling or compaction are where rust first appears in a damp cable; ultra-high-strength wire with poor ductility can break brittly where it bends locally at saddles or bands, hidden inside the cable. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：鍍層是犧牲性防蝕，架設時的刮傷會成為日後腐蝕的起點。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The coating is sacrificial, and scratches during erection become future corrosion sites.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鍍鋅只是外觀處理，對主纜壽命影響不大。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Galvanising is cosmetic and hardly affects cable life.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"鍍鋅層在牽引或擠壓時被大面積刮除，日後在纜內潮濕環境中最先出現鏽點；超高強度鋼絲若延性不足，在索鞍或索夾附近的局部彎曲處可能脆斷，而且斷絲藏在纜內不易被發現。","textEn":"Large areas of zinc scraped off during hauling or compaction are where rust first appears in a damp cable; ultra-high-strength wire with poor ductility can break brittly where it bends locally at saddles or bands, hidden inside the cable.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「主纜鋼絲的強度等級與鍍層」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Strength grades and coatings of cable wire\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["鍍鋅層在牽引或擠壓時被大面積刮除，日後在纜內潮濕環境中最先出現鏽點；超高強度鋼絲若延性不足，在索鞍或索夾附近的局部彎曲處可能脆斷，而且斷絲藏在纜內不易被發現。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","鋼絲只承受軸向拉力，索鞍形狀不影響應力。"],"optionsEn":["Large areas of zinc scraped off during hauling or compaction are where rust first appears in a damp cable.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Cable wires carry only axial tension, so saddle shape does not affect stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鍍鋅層在牽引或擠壓時被大面積刮除，日後在纜內潮濕環境中最先出現鏽點；超高強度鋼絲若延性不足，在索鞍或索夾附近的局部彎曲處可能脆斷，而且斷絲藏在纜內不易被發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Large areas of zinc scraped off during hauling or compaction are where rust first appears in a damp cable; ultra-high-strength wire with poor ductility can break brittly where it bends locally at saddles or bands, hidden inside the cable. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b036-v13-13","title":"索鞍、分束與錨固細部：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Saddles, splay and anchorage details: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「索鞍半徑與彎曲應力」如何影響懸索橋主纜架設的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Saddle radius and bending stress” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-bridge main-cable erection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主纜在塔頂索鞍處改變方向，在錨碇前的分束鞍處散開成一束束，再以索靴（空中紡線）或錨頭（預製索股）連接到錨碇拉桿。鋼絲繞過彎曲面時，除了軸向應力外還有與曲率成正比的彎曲應力，並在接觸面上承受側壓與摩擦；索鞍槽的半徑、隔板與填充材決定這些附加應力的大小，也決定主纜在索鞍內是否會滑動。分束處的鋼絲排列若與錨固點對不上，部分鋼絲會被拉長、部分鬆弛。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「索鞍半徑與彎曲應力」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The main cable changes direction at the tower-top saddles and fans out at splay saddles in front of the anchorages, where bundles connect to anchor rods through strand shoes (aerial spinning) or sockets (PWS). Where wires pass over a curved surface they carry bending stress proportional to curvature on top of axial stress, plus side pressure and friction at the contact; saddle groove radius, spacers and fillers set the size of these extra stresses and whether the cable slips in the saddle. If the wire arrangement at the splay does not match the anchorage points, some wires are stretched and others go slack. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Saddle radius and bending stress” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：鋼絲繞過半徑 R 的彎曲面時，表面彎曲應力 σ_b = E·d/(2R)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A wire bent over radius R has surface bending stress σ_b = E·d/(2R).","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼絲只承受軸向拉力，索鞍形狀不影響應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cable wires carry only axial tension, so saddle shape does not affect stress.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「索鞍半徑與彎曲應力」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Saddle radius and bending stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-13-k1","title":"索鞍、分束與錨固細部","titleEn":"Saddles, splay and anchorage details","text":"主纜在塔頂索鞍處改變方向，在錨碇前的分束鞍處散開成一束束，再以索靴（空中紡線）或錨頭（預製索股）連接到錨碇拉桿。鋼絲繞過彎曲面時，除了軸向應力外還有與曲率成正比的彎曲應力，並在接觸面上承受側壓與摩擦；索鞍槽的半徑、隔板與填充材決定這些附加應力的大小，也決定主纜在索鞍內是否會滑動。","textEn":"The main cable changes direction at the tower-top saddles and fans out at splay saddles in front of the anchorages, where bundles connect to anchor rods through strand shoes (aerial spinning) or sockets (PWS). Where wires pass over a curved surface they carry bending stress proportional to curvature on top of axial stress, plus side pressure and friction at the contact; saddle groove radius, spacers and fillers set the size of these extra stresses and whether the cable slips in the saddle.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼絲只承受軸向拉力，索鞍形狀不影響應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cable wires carry only axial tension, so saddle shape does not affect stress. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「索鞍、分束與錨固細部」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Saddles, splay and anchorage details\" is correct?","options":["鋼絲只承受軸向拉力，索鞍形狀不影響應力。","主纜在塔頂索鞍處改變方向，在錨碇前的分束鞍處散開成一束束，再以索靴（空中紡線）或錨頭（預製索股）連接到錨碇拉桿。","貓道只是臨時走道，可以用一般鷹架的標準設計。"],"optionsEn":["Cable wires carry only axial tension, so saddle shape does not affect stress.","The main cable changes direction at the tower-top saddles and fans out at splay saddles in front of the anchorages, where bundles connect to anchor rods through strand shoes (aerial spinning) or sockets (PWS).","A catwalk is only a temporary walkway and can be designed like ordinary scaffolding."],"answer":1,"explanation":"主纜在塔頂索鞍處改變方向，在錨碇前的分束鞍處散開成一束束，再以索靴（空中紡線）或錨頭（預製索股）連接到錨碇拉桿。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The main cable changes direction at the tower-top saddles and fans out at splay saddles in front of the anchorages, where bundles connect to anchor rods through strand shoes (aerial spinning) or sockets (PWS). The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b036-v13-14","title":"索鞍、分束與錨固細部：定量估算","titleEn":"Saddles, splay and anchorage details: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「索鞍半徑與彎曲應力」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Saddle radius and bending stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：鋼絲繞過半徑 R 的彎曲面時，表面彎曲應力 σ_b = E·d/(2R)。取 E = 200,000 N/mm²、d = 5.4 mm：R = 3.0 m 時 σ_b = 200,000×5.4/6,000 = 180 N/mm²；R = 1.0 m 時增為 540 N/mm²，加上約 700 N/mm² 的軸向應力就逼近降伏。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A wire bent over radius R has surface bending stress σ_b = E·d/(2R). With E = 200,000 N/mm² and d = 5.4 mm: R = 3.0 m gives σ_b = 200,000×5.4/6,000 = 180 N/mm²; R = 1.0 m gives 540 N/mm², which on top of about 700 N/mm² axial stress approaches yield. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：索鞍與分束鞍以鑄造或焊接製造後，量測槽半徑、隔板位置與表面粗糙度，並以全尺寸或縮尺模型試驗確認抗滑係數；錨頭（澆鑄鋅或環氧樹脂鋼球）抽樣做靜力與疲勞拉拔試驗，記錄錨頭回縮量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After casting or welding saddles and splay saddles, measure groove radius, spacer positions and surface roughness, and confirm slip resistance by full- or reduced-scale tests; sample sockets, whether zinc-cast or epoxy–steel-ball, for static and fatigue pull-out tests, recording socket draw-in.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"鋼絲繞過半徑 R 的彎曲面時，表面彎曲應力 σ_b = E·d/(2R)。取 E = 200,000 N/mm²、d = 5.4 mm：R = 3.0 m 時 σ_b = 200,000×5.4/6,000 = 180 N/mm²；R = 1.0 m 時增為 540 N/mm²，加上約 700 N/mm² 的軸向應力就逼近降伏。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A wire bent over radius R has surface bending stress σ_b = E·d/(2R). With E = 200,000 N/mm² and d = 5.4 mm: R = 3.0 m gives σ_b = 200,000×5.4/6,000 = 180 N/mm²; R = 1.0 m gives 540 N/mm², which on top of about 700 N/mm² axial stress approaches yield. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「索鞍、分束與錨固細部」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Saddles, splay and anchorage details\", which statement holds?","options":["儀器越精密，就不需要相對量測與交叉核對。","主纜外觀完好、塗裝沒有剝落，內部鋼絲就一定沒有腐蝕。","鋼絲繞過半徑 R 的彎曲面時，表面彎曲應力 σ_b = E·d/(2R)。"],"optionsEn":["With precise enough instruments, relative measurement and cross-checks are unnecessary.","If the cable looks sound and its paint is intact, the wires inside cannot be corroded.","A wire bent over radius R has surface bending stress σ_b = E·d/(2R)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鋼絲繞過半徑 R 的彎曲面時，表面彎曲應力 σ_b = E·d/(2R)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A wire bent over radius R has surface bending stress σ_b = E·d/(2R). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b036-v13-15","title":"索鞍、分束與錨固細部：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Saddles, splay and anchorage details: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「索鞍半徑與彎曲應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Saddle radius and bending stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"索鞍與分束鞍以鑄造或焊接製造後，量測槽半徑、隔板位置與表面粗糙度，並以全尺寸或縮尺模型試驗確認抗滑係數；錨頭（澆鑄鋅或環氧樹脂鋼球）抽樣做靜力與疲勞拉拔試驗，記錄錨頭回縮量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After casting or welding saddles and splay saddles, measure groove radius, spacer positions and surface roughness, and confirm slip resistance by full- or reduced-scale tests; sample sockets, whether zinc-cast or epoxy–steel-ball, for static and fatigue pull-out tests, recording socket draw-in. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：索鞍、分束鞍與錨固細部應在設計圖中標明最小彎曲半徑、鋼絲排列圖與抗滑檢核，並把錨頭試驗、錨頭回縮量與錨固位置列為停留點；完工後保留可目視錨頭與索靴的檢查通道。","observationEn":"Site practice: Drawings for saddles, splay saddles and anchorage details should show minimum bending radius, wire arrangement and slip checks, with socket tests, draw-in and anchorage positions as hold points; keep inspection access to see sockets and strand shoes after completion.","failure":"注意干擾：索鞍槽半徑過小或邊緣倒角不足，鋼絲在長期車流與溫度循環下於彎曲處疲勞斷絲；鞍內填充不實時，主纜在不平衡荷重下滑動，改變兩側垂度並損傷鍍層；錨頭灌注不良則可能使鋼絲從錨頭拔出。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A saddle groove with too small a radius or poor edge rounding lets wires fatigue and break at the bend under years of traffic and thermal cycles; incomplete filling in the saddle lets the cable slip under unbalanced load, changing sags on both sides and damaging coating; poorly filled sockets can let wires pull out. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"索鞍與分束鞍以鑄造或焊接製造後，量測槽半徑、隔板位置與表面粗糙度，並以全尺寸或縮尺模型試驗確認抗滑係數；錨頭（澆鑄鋅或環氧樹脂鋼球）抽樣做靜力與疲勞拉拔試驗，記錄錨頭回縮量。","textEn":"After casting or welding saddles and splay saddles, measure groove radius, spacer positions and surface roughness, and confirm slip resistance by full- or reduced-scale tests; sample sockets, whether zinc-cast or epoxy–steel-ball, for static and fatigue pull-out tests, recording socket draw-in.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"索鞍、分束鞍與錨固細部應在設計圖中標明最小彎曲半徑、鋼絲排列圖與抗滑檢核，並把錨頭試驗、錨頭回縮量與錨固位置列為停留點；完工後保留可目視錨頭與索靴的檢查通道。","textEn":"Drawings for saddles, splay saddles and anchorage details should show minimum bending radius, wire arrangement and slip checks, with socket tests, draw-in and anchorage positions as hold points; keep inspection access to see sockets and strand shoes after completion.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「索鞍、分束與錨固細部」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Saddles, splay and anchorage details\"?","options":["索鞍與分束鞍以鑄造或焊接製造後，量測槽半徑、隔板位置與表面粗糙度，並以全尺寸或縮尺模型試驗確認抗滑係數。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","預製索股一定比空中紡線先進，任何橋都應該使用。"],"optionsEn":["After casting or welding saddles and splay saddles, measure groove radius, spacer positions and surface roughness, and confirm slip resistance by full- or reduced-scale tests.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Prefabricated strands are always more advanced and should be used on every bridge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"索鞍與分束鞍以鑄造或焊接製造後，量測槽半徑、隔板位置與表面粗糙度，並以全尺寸或縮尺模型試驗確認抗滑係數；錨頭（澆鑄鋅或環氧樹脂鋼球）抽樣做靜力與疲勞拉拔試驗，記錄錨頭回縮量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After casting or welding saddles and splay saddles, measure groove radius, spacer positions and surface roughness, and confirm slip resistance by full- or reduced-scale tests; sample sockets, whether zinc-cast or epoxy–steel-ball, for static and fatigue pull-out tests, recording socket draw-in. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b036-v13-16","title":"索鞍、分束與錨固細部：失效診斷","titleEn":"Saddles, splay and anchorage details: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「索鞍半徑與彎曲應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Saddle radius and bending stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"索鞍槽半徑過小或邊緣倒角不足，鋼絲在長期車流與溫度循環下於彎曲處疲勞斷絲；鞍內填充不實時，主纜在不平衡荷重下滑動，改變兩側垂度並損傷鍍層；錨頭灌注不良則可能使鋼絲從錨頭拔出。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A saddle groove with too small a radius or poor edge rounding lets wires fatigue and break at the bend under years of traffic and thermal cycles; incomplete filling in the saddle lets the cable slip under unbalanced load, changing sags on both sides and damaging coating; poorly filled sockets can let wires pull out. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：分束處的鋼絲排列若與錨固點對不上，部分鋼絲會被拉長、部分鬆弛。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If the wire arrangement at the splay does not match the anchorage points, some wires are stretched and others go slack.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼絲只承受軸向拉力，索鞍形狀不影響應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cable wires carry only axial tension, so saddle shape does not affect stress.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"索鞍槽半徑過小或邊緣倒角不足，鋼絲在長期車流與溫度循環下於彎曲處疲勞斷絲；鞍內填充不實時，主纜在不平衡荷重下滑動，改變兩側垂度並損傷鍍層；錨頭灌注不良則可能使鋼絲從錨頭拔出。","textEn":"A saddle groove with too small a radius or poor edge rounding lets wires fatigue and break at the bend under years of traffic and thermal cycles; incomplete filling in the saddle lets the cable slip under unbalanced load, changing sags on both sides and damaging coating; poorly filled sockets can let wires pull out.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「索鞍、分束與錨固細部」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Saddles, splay and anchorage details\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","索鞍槽半徑過小或邊緣倒角不足，鋼絲在長期車流與溫度循環下於彎曲處疲勞斷絲。","貓道只是臨時走道，可以用一般鷹架的標準設計。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A saddle groove with too small a radius or poor edge rounding lets wires fatigue and break at the bend under years of traffic and thermal cycles.","A catwalk is only a temporary walkway and can be designed like ordinary scaffolding."],"answer":1,"explanation":"索鞍槽半徑過小或邊緣倒角不足，鋼絲在長期車流與溫度循環下於彎曲處疲勞斷絲；鞍內填充不實時，主纜在不平衡荷重下滑動，改變兩側垂度並損傷鍍層；錨頭灌注不良則可能使鋼絲從錨頭拔出。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A saddle groove with too small a radius or poor edge rounding lets wires fatigue and break at the bend under years of traffic and thermal cycles; incomplete filling in the saddle lets the cable slip under unbalanced load, changing sags on both sides and damaging coating; poorly filled sockets can let wires pull out. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b036-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「導索、貓道與牽引系統」與「主纜擠壓、纏絲與索夾安裝」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pilot rope, catwalk and hauling system\" and \"Compaction, wrapping and cable-band installation\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b036-v13-17","title":"導索、貓道與牽引系統：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Pilot rope, catwalk and hauling system: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「導索跨越與貓道」如何影響懸索橋主纜架設的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pilot-rope crossing and catwalk” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-bridge main-cable erection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主纜架設的第一步是把一條細導索跨過兩座塔：早期做法是讓導索浮在浮筒上以船拖過，必須封閉航道；瀨戶大橋改以起重船把導索吊高跨越，本州四國連絡橋在潮流強、船多的海域也以直升機牽引導索。導索就位後依序拉上較粗的鋼索，架成貓道：瀨戶大橋的貓道由約 10 條鋼索承托，鋪鋼絲網與雙層纖維網，寬 4.5 m、扶手高 1.4 m，並以橫向便橋連接。貓道本身就是一座臨時懸索橋，其線形必須與主纜平行，並能承受作業荷重與強風。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「導索跨越與貓道」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The first step of cable erection is to get a thin pilot rope across the two towers: the old way floated it on buoys and towed it across by boat, closing the channel; Seto Ohashi held it high from a crane ship instead, and in Honshu-Shikoku waters with strong currents and heavy traffic it was also flown across by helicopter. Heavier ropes are then pulled across in turn to build the catwalk: Seto Ohashi's catwalks rested on about ten ropes with wire mesh and a double fibre net, 4.5 m wide with 1.4 m handrails, linked by cross-bridges. A catwalk is itself a temporary suspension bridge whose profile must parallel the main cable and carry working loads and strong wind. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Pilot-rope crossing and catwalk” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：貓道承載索水平張力 H = w·l²/(8f)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Catwalk rope horizontal tension H = w·l²/(8f).","failure":"常見誤解：「貓道只是臨時走道，可以用一般鷹架的標準設計。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A catwalk is only a temporary walkway and can be designed like ordinary scaffolding.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「導索跨越與貓道」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Pilot-rope crossing and catwalk”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-17-k1","title":"導索、貓道與牽引系統","titleEn":"Pilot rope, catwalk and hauling system","text":"主纜架設的第一步是把一條細導索跨過兩座塔：早期做法是讓導索浮在浮筒上以船拖過，必須封閉航道；瀨戶大橋改以起重船把導索吊高跨越，本州四國連絡橋在潮流強、船多的海域也以直升機牽引導索。導索就位後依序拉上較粗的鋼索，架成貓道：瀨戶大橋的貓道由約 10 條鋼索承托，鋪鋼絲網與雙層纖維網，寬 4.5 m、扶手高 1.4 m，並以橫向便橋連接。","textEn":"The first step of cable erection is to get a thin pilot rope across the two towers: the old way floated it on buoys and towed it across by boat, closing the channel; Seto Ohashi held it high from a crane ship instead, and in Honshu-Shikoku waters with strong currents and heavy traffic it was also flown across by helicopter. Heavier ropes are then pulled across in turn to build the catwalk: Seto Ohashi's catwalks rested on about ten ropes with wire mesh and a double fibre net, 4.5 m wide with 1.4 m handrails, linked by cross-bridges.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：貓道只是臨時走道，可以用一般鷹架的標準設計。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A catwalk is only a temporary walkway and can be designed like ordinary scaffolding. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「導索、貓道與牽引系統」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pilot rope, catwalk and hauling system\" is correct?","options":["貓道只是臨時走道，可以用一般鷹架的標準設計。","主纜擠壓只是為了外觀圓整，對耐久性影響不大。","主纜架設的第一步是把一條細導索跨過兩座塔：早期做法是讓導索浮在浮筒上以船拖過，必須封閉航道。"],"optionsEn":["A catwalk is only a temporary walkway and can be designed like ordinary scaffolding.","Compaction is only to make the cable look round and hardly affects durability.","The first step of cable erection is to get a thin pilot rope across the two towers: the old way floated it on buoys and towed it across by boat, closing the channel."],"answer":2,"explanation":"主纜架設的第一步是把一條細導索跨過兩座塔：早期做法是讓導索浮在浮筒上以船拖過，必須封閉航道；瀨戶大橋改以起重船把導索吊高跨越，本州四國連絡橋在潮流強、船多的海域也以直升機牽引導索。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The first step of cable erection is to get a thin pilot rope across the two towers: the old way floated it on buoys and towed it across by boat, closing the channel; Seto Ohashi held it high from a crane ship instead, and in Honshu-Shikoku waters with strong currents and heavy traffic it was also flown across by helicopter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b036-v13-18","title":"導索、貓道與牽引系統：定量估算","titleEn":"Pilot rope, catwalk and hauling system: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「導索跨越與貓道」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pilot-rope crossing and catwalk” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：貓道承載索水平張力 H = w·l²/(8f)。取每座貓道自重加作業荷重 w = 1.2 kN/m、跨徑 l = 1,500 m、垂度 f = 150 m：H = 1.2×1,500²/(8×150) = 2,250 kN；若分由 10 條鋼索承擔，每條約 225 kN。垂度若減為 140 m，H 增為約 2,411 kN。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Catwalk rope horizontal tension H = w·l²/(8f). With self-weight plus working load w = 1.2 kN/m per catwalk, span l = 1,500 m and sag f = 150 m: H = 1.2×1,500²/(8×150) = 2,250 kN, about 225 kN for each of ten ropes. Reducing the sag to 140 m raises H to about 2,411 kN. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：導索跨越前取得海事主管機關的作業許可與航行警告，跨越時量測導索最低點高程；貓道完成後檢查網片、扶手與橫向便橋的固定，量測貓道線形與主纜設計線形的間距，並以風速計設定作業與撤離門檻。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before the crossing obtain marine-authority approval and a navigation warning, measuring the rope's lowest point during the crossing; after the catwalk is built inspect mesh, handrails and cross-bridge fixings, measure the gap between catwalk profile and the design cable profile, and set work and evacuation thresholds with anemometers.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"貓道承載索水平張力 H = w·l²/(8f)。取每座貓道自重加作業荷重 w = 1.2 kN/m、跨徑 l = 1,500 m、垂度 f = 150 m：H = 1.2×1,500²/(8×150) = 2,250 kN；若分由 10 條鋼索承擔，每條約 225 kN。垂度若減為 140 m，H 增為約 2,411 kN。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Catwalk rope horizontal tension H = w·l²/(8f). With self-weight plus working load w = 1.2 kN/m per catwalk, span l = 1,500 m and sag f = 150 m: H = 1.2×1,500²/(8×150) = 2,250 kN, about 225 kN for each of ten ropes. Reducing the sag to 140 m raises H to about 2,411 kN. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「導索、貓道與牽引系統」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pilot rope, catwalk and hauling system\", which statement holds?","options":["貓道承載索水平張力 H = w·l²/(8f)。","只要平均強度高於規格，整批鋼絲就合格。","主纜強度在完工時就確定，之後只需目視檢查外觀。"],"optionsEn":["Catwalk rope horizontal tension H = w·l²/(8f).","If the mean strength is above specification, the whole lot passes.","Cable strength is fixed at completion, so only visual checks of the outside are needed afterwards."],"answer":0,"explanation":"貓道承載索水平張力 H = w·l²/(8f)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Catwalk rope horizontal tension H = w·l²/(8f). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b036-v13-19","title":"導索、貓道與牽引系統：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pilot rope, catwalk and hauling system: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「導索跨越與貓道」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pilot-rope crossing and catwalk” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"導索跨越前取得海事主管機關的作業許可與航行警告，跨越時量測導索最低點高程；貓道完成後檢查網片、扶手與橫向便橋的固定，量測貓道線形與主纜設計線形的間距，並以風速計設定作業與撤離門檻。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before the crossing obtain marine-authority approval and a navigation warning, measuring the rope's lowest point during the crossing; after the catwalk is built inspect mesh, handrails and cross-bridge fixings, measure the gap between catwalk profile and the design cable profile, and set work and evacuation thresholds with anemometers. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：貓道屬於臨時結構，須有獨立設計計算、抗風穩定檢核、每日檢查表與撤離程序，並由臨時工程設計者簽認；牽引系統的最大拉力、制動與通訊要在試運轉中驗證後才可牽引第一股。","observationEn":"Site practice: A catwalk is temporary works needing its own design calculations, wind-stability check, daily checklist and evacuation procedure signed by the temporary-works designer; the hauling system's maximum pull, braking and communications must be proven in a trial run before the first strand is hauled.","failure":"注意干擾：導索在跨越時下垂進入航道淨空可能勾到船舶；貓道與主纜線形不平行，鋼絲在某些區段會摩擦網片或被迫偏折；強風中貓道過度擺動，曾在多座橋的施工中造成停工與設備損壞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A pilot rope sagging into the navigation clearance can snag a ship; a catwalk not parallel to the cable makes wires rub the mesh or bend in places; excessive catwalk sway in strong wind has stopped work and damaged equipment on many bridge projects. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"導索跨越前取得海事主管機關的作業許可與航行警告，跨越時量測導索最低點高程；貓道完成後檢查網片、扶手與橫向便橋的固定，量測貓道線形與主纜設計線形的間距，並以風速計設定作業與撤離門檻。","textEn":"Before the crossing obtain marine-authority approval and a navigation warning, measuring the rope's lowest point during the crossing; after the catwalk is built inspect mesh, handrails and cross-bridge fixings, measure the gap between catwalk profile and the design cable profile, and set work and evacuation thresholds with anemometers.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"貓道屬於臨時結構，須有獨立設計計算、抗風穩定檢核、每日檢查表與撤離程序，並由臨時工程設計者簽認；牽引系統的最大拉力、制動與通訊要在試運轉中驗證後才可牽引第一股。","textEn":"A catwalk is temporary works needing its own design calculations, wind-stability check, daily checklist and evacuation procedure signed by the temporary-works designer; the hauling system's maximum pull, braking and communications must be proven in a trial run before the first strand is hauled.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「導索、貓道與牽引系統」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pilot rope, catwalk and hauling system\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","導索跨越前取得海事主管機關的作業許可與航行警告，跨越時量測導索最低點高程。","主纜在任何階段都是拋物線，差別可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Before the crossing obtain marine-authority approval and a navigation warning, measuring the rope's lowest point during the crossing.","The cable is a parabola at every stage, and the difference is negligible."],"answer":1,"explanation":"導索跨越前取得海事主管機關的作業許可與航行警告，跨越時量測導索最低點高程；貓道完成後檢查網片、扶手與橫向便橋的固定，量測貓道線形與主纜設計線形的間距，並以風速計設定作業與撤離門檻。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before the crossing obtain marine-authority approval and a navigation warning, measuring the rope's lowest point during the crossing; after the catwalk is built inspect mesh, handrails and cross-bridge fixings, measure the gap between catwalk profile and the design cable profile, and set work and evacuation thresholds with anemometers. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b036-v13-20","title":"導索、貓道與牽引系統：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pilot rope, catwalk and hauling system: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「導索跨越與貓道」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pilot-rope crossing and catwalk” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"導索在跨越時下垂進入航道淨空可能勾到船舶；貓道與主纜線形不平行，鋼絲在某些區段會摩擦網片或被迫偏折；強風中貓道過度擺動，曾在多座橋的施工中造成停工與設備損壞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A pilot rope sagging into the navigation clearance can snag a ship; a catwalk not parallel to the cable makes wires rub the mesh or bend in places; excessive catwalk sway in strong wind has stopped work and damaged equipment on many bridge projects. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：貓道本身就是一座臨時懸索橋，其線形必須與主纜平行，並能承受作業荷重與強風。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A catwalk is itself a temporary suspension bridge whose profile must parallel the main cable and carry working loads and strong wind.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「貓道只是臨時走道，可以用一般鷹架的標準設計。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A catwalk is only a temporary walkway and can be designed like ordinary scaffolding.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"導索在跨越時下垂進入航道淨空可能勾到船舶；貓道與主纜線形不平行，鋼絲在某些區段會摩擦網片或被迫偏折；強風中貓道過度擺動，曾在多座橋的施工中造成停工與設備損壞。","textEn":"A pilot rope sagging into the navigation clearance can snag a ship; a catwalk not parallel to the cable makes wires rub the mesh or bend in places; excessive catwalk sway in strong wind has stopped work and damaged equipment on many bridge projects.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導索、貓道與牽引系統」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pilot rope, catwalk and hauling system\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","主纜擠壓只是為了外觀圓整，對耐久性影響不大。","導索在跨越時下垂進入航道淨空可能勾到船舶；貓道與主纜線形不平行，鋼絲在某些區段會摩擦網片或被迫偏折；強風中貓道過度擺動，曾在多座橋的施工中造成停工與設備損壞。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Compaction is only to make the cable look round and hardly affects durability.","A pilot rope sagging into the navigation clearance can snag a ship."],"answer":2,"explanation":"導索在跨越時下垂進入航道淨空可能勾到船舶；貓道與主纜線形不平行，鋼絲在某些區段會摩擦網片或被迫偏折；強風中貓道過度擺動，曾在多座橋的施工中造成停工與設備損壞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A pilot rope sagging into the navigation clearance can snag a ship; a catwalk not parallel to the cable makes wires rub the mesh or bend in places; excessive catwalk sway in strong wind has stopped work and damaged equipment on many bridge projects. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b036-v13-21","title":"主纜擠壓、纏絲與索夾安裝：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Compaction, wrapping and cable-band installation: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「擠壓與纏絲」如何影響懸索橋主纜架設的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Compaction and wrapping” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-bridge main-cable erection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"所有鋼絲架好後，主纜還是由許多六角形或圓形的束鬆散組成，需要以液壓擠壓機沿全長逐段把它壓成接近圓形的緊密斷面，並暫時以鋼帶綁住。擠壓品質決定空隙率：空隙太大，水分容易進入並滯留在纜內；擠壓不均則讓索夾無法均勻夾緊。之後安裝索夾（兩個半圓柱以螺栓夾緊，坡度越陡需要越多螺栓），掛上吊索，最後以纏絲機把鍍鋅軟鋼線（美國常用 No. 9 線）緊密纏繞在主纜外，並塗上防蝕膏與塗料，或改用彈性體包覆配合乾燥空氣。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「擠壓與纏絲」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Once all wires are in place, the cable is still a loose group of hexagonal or round bundles, and hydraulic compactors work along its length to press it into a dense, nearly round section, temporarily banded with steel straps. Compaction sets the void ratio: too many voids let water enter and stay in the cable, and uneven compaction stops cable bands from clamping evenly. Cable bands are then installed, two half-cylinders bolted together, with more bolts on steeper slopes, the hangers are hung, and finally a wrapping machine winds soft galvanised wire (No. 9 wire in US practice) tightly around the cable over a corrosion-inhibiting paste and paint, or an elastomeric wrap is used with dry air. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Compaction and wrapping” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：主纜直徑 D = √[4·N·a/(π·(1 − v))]。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Cable diameter D = √[4·N·a/(π·(1 − v))].","failure":"常見誤解：「主纜擠壓只是為了外觀圓整，對耐久性影響不大。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Compaction is only to make the cable look round and hardly affects durability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「擠壓與纏絲」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Compaction and wrapping”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-21-k1","title":"主纜擠壓、纏絲與索夾安裝","titleEn":"Compaction, wrapping and cable-band installation","text":"所有鋼絲架好後，主纜還是由許多六角形或圓形的束鬆散組成，需要以液壓擠壓機沿全長逐段把它壓成接近圓形的緊密斷面，並暫時以鋼帶綁住。擠壓品質決定空隙率：空隙太大，水分容易進入並滯留在纜內；擠壓不均則讓索夾無法均勻夾緊。","textEn":"Once all wires are in place, the cable is still a loose group of hexagonal or round bundles, and hydraulic compactors work along its length to press it into a dense, nearly round section, temporarily banded with steel straps. Compaction sets the void ratio: too many voids let water enter and stay in the cable, and uneven compaction stops cable bands from clamping evenly.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：主纜擠壓只是為了外觀圓整，對耐久性影響不大。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Compaction is only to make the cable look round and hardly affects durability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「主纜擠壓、纏絲與索夾安裝」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Compaction, wrapping and cable-band installation\" is correct?","options":["所有鋼絲架好後，主纜還是由許多六角形或圓形的束鬆散組成，需要以液壓擠壓機沿全長逐段把它壓成接近圓形的緊密斷面，並暫時以鋼帶綁住。","主纜擠壓只是為了外觀圓整，對耐久性影響不大。","儀器越精密，就不需要相對量測與交叉核對。"],"optionsEn":["Once all wires are in place, the cable is still a loose group of hexagonal or round bundles, and hydraulic compactors work along its length to press it into a dense, nearly round section, temporarily banded with steel straps.","Compaction is only to make the cable look round and hardly affects durability.","With precise enough instruments, relative measurement and cross-checks are unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"所有鋼絲架好後，主纜還是由許多六角形或圓形的束鬆散組成，需要以液壓擠壓機沿全長逐段把它壓成接近圓形的緊密斷面，並暫時以鋼帶綁住。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Once all wires are in place, the cable is still a loose group of hexagonal or round bundles, and hydraulic compactors work along its length to press it into a dense, nearly round section, temporarily banded with steel straps. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b036-v13-22","title":"主纜擠壓、纏絲與索夾安裝：定量估算","titleEn":"Compaction, wrapping and cable-band installation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「擠壓與纏絲」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Compaction and wrapping” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：主纜直徑 D = √[4·N·a/(π·(1 − v))]。取 18,000 根 5.4 mm 鋼絲，a = 22.90 mm²，鋼絲面積 0.4122 m²：空隙率 v = 18% 時 D ≈ √(4×0.4122/(π×0.82)) ≈ 0.800 m；v = 22% 時 D ≈ 0.820 m。直徑差 20 mm 就代表索夾內徑與螺栓夾緊量需要重新核對。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Cable diameter D = √[4·N·a/(π·(1 − v))]. With 18,000 wires of 5.4 mm, a = 22.90 mm² and a steel area of 0.4122 m²: a void ratio v = 18% gives D ≈ √(4×0.4122/(π×0.82)) ≈ 0.800 m, while v = 22% gives D ≈ 0.820 m. A 20 mm difference means cable-band bore and bolt clamping must be re-checked. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：擠壓後沿全長以周長尺或雷射量測直徑與橢圓度，換算空隙率並與允收範圍比較；索夾安裝時依程序分次張拉螺栓並記錄，纏絲時量測纏絲張力、搭接與間距，逐段拍照存檔。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After compaction measure diameter and ovality along the length with a circumference tape or laser, convert to void ratio and compare with the acceptance range; tension cable-band bolts in stages per procedure and record them, and during wrapping measure wrapping tension, laps and pitch, photographing each section for the record.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"主纜直徑 D = √[4·N·a/(π·(1 − v))]。取 18,000 根 5.4 mm 鋼絲，a = 22.90 mm²，鋼絲面積 0.4122 m²：空隙率 v = 18% 時 D ≈ √(4×0.4122/(π×0.82)) ≈ 0.800 m；v = 22% 時 D ≈ 0.820 m。直徑差 20 mm 就代表索夾內徑與螺栓夾緊量需要重新核對。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Cable diameter D = √[4·N·a/(π·(1 − v))]. With 18,000 wires of 5.4 mm, a = 22.90 mm² and a steel area of 0.4122 m²: a void ratio v = 18% gives D ≈ √(4×0.4122/(π×0.82)) ≈ 0.800 m, while v = 22% gives D ≈ 0.820 m. A 20 mm difference means cable-band bore and bolt clamping must be re-checked. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「主纜擠壓、纏絲與索夾安裝」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Compaction, wrapping and cable-band installation\", which statement holds?","options":["主纜外觀完好、塗裝沒有剝落，內部鋼絲就一定沒有腐蝕。","主纜直徑 D = √[4·N·a/(π·(1 − v))]。","預製索股一定比空中紡線先進，任何橋都應該使用。"],"optionsEn":["If the cable looks sound and its paint is intact, the wires inside cannot be corroded.","Cable diameter D = √[4·N·a/(π·(1 − v))].","Prefabricated strands are always more advanced and should be used on every bridge."],"answer":1,"explanation":"主纜直徑 D = √[4·N·a/(π·(1 − v))]。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Cable diameter D = √[4·N·a/(π·(1 − v))]. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b036-v13-23","title":"主纜擠壓、纏絲與索夾安裝：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Compaction, wrapping and cable-band installation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「擠壓與纏絲」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Compaction and wrapping” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"擠壓後沿全長以周長尺或雷射量測直徑與橢圓度，換算空隙率並與允收範圍比較；索夾安裝時依程序分次張拉螺栓並記錄，纏絲時量測纏絲張力、搭接與間距，逐段拍照存檔。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After compaction measure diameter and ovality along the length with a circumference tape or laser, convert to void ratio and compare with the acceptance range; tension cable-band bolts in stages per procedure and record them, and during wrapping measure wrapping tension, laps and pitch, photographing each section for the record. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：擠壓與纏絲應列為逐段驗收項目，直徑、空隙率、螺栓張力與纏絲紀錄須能追溯到區段編號；索夾螺栓應在完工後一定期間（例如數月內）複測一次預力，以補償初期壓密造成的損失。","observationEn":"Site practice: Make compaction and wrapping section-by-section acceptance items, with diameter, void ratio, bolt tension and wrapping records traceable to section numbers; re-check cable-band bolt preload within a set period after completion, for example within a few months, to make up for losses from early consolidation.","failure":"注意干擾：擠壓不足的區段在完工後仍持續壓密，索夾螺栓預力隨之流失，索夾可能下滑；纏絲間隙或防蝕膏不連續處成為水分入口，主纜低點與索夾下方最先出現腐蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Under-compacted sections keep consolidating after completion, so cable-band bolt preload is lost and bands may slip; gaps in wrapping or breaks in the paste become water entry points, and corrosion appears first at cable low points and under bands. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"擠壓後沿全長以周長尺或雷射量測直徑與橢圓度，換算空隙率並與允收範圍比較；索夾安裝時依程序分次張拉螺栓並記錄，纏絲時量測纏絲張力、搭接與間距，逐段拍照存檔。","textEn":"After compaction measure diameter and ovality along the length with a circumference tape or laser, convert to void ratio and compare with the acceptance range; tension cable-band bolts in stages per procedure and record them, and during wrapping measure wrapping tension, laps and pitch, photographing each section for the record.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"擠壓與纏絲應列為逐段驗收項目，直徑、空隙率、螺栓張力與纏絲紀錄須能追溯到區段編號；索夾螺栓應在完工後一定期間（例如數月內）複測一次預力，以補償初期壓密造成的損失。","textEn":"Make compaction and wrapping section-by-section acceptance items, with diameter, void ratio, bolt tension and wrapping records traceable to section numbers; re-check cable-band bolt preload within a set period after completion, for example within a few months, to make up for losses from early consolidation.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「主纜擠壓、纏絲與索夾安裝」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Compaction, wrapping and cable-band installation\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","鍍鋅只是外觀處理，對主纜壽命影響不大。","擠壓後沿全長以周長尺或雷射量測直徑與橢圓度，換算空隙率並與允收範圍比較；索夾安裝時依程序分次張拉螺栓並記錄，纏絲時量測纏絲張力、搭接與間距，逐段拍照存檔。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Galvanising is cosmetic and hardly affects cable life.","After compaction measure diameter and ovality along the length with a circumference tape or laser, convert to void ratio and compare with the acceptance range."],"answer":2,"explanation":"擠壓後沿全長以周長尺或雷射量測直徑與橢圓度，換算空隙率並與允收範圍比較；索夾安裝時依程序分次張拉螺栓並記錄，纏絲時量測纏絲張力、搭接與間距，逐段拍照存檔。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After compaction measure diameter and ovality along the length with a circumference tape or laser, convert to void ratio and compare with the acceptance range; tension cable-band bolts in stages per procedure and record them, and during wrapping measure wrapping tension, laps and pitch, photographing each section for the record. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b036-v13-24","title":"主纜擠壓、纏絲與索夾安裝：失效診斷","titleEn":"Compaction, wrapping and cable-band installation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「擠壓與纏絲」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Compaction and wrapping” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"擠壓不足的區段在完工後仍持續壓密，索夾螺栓預力隨之流失，索夾可能下滑；纏絲間隙或防蝕膏不連續處成為水分入口，主纜低點與索夾下方最先出現腐蝕。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Under-compacted sections keep consolidating after completion, so cable-band bolt preload is lost and bands may slip; gaps in wrapping or breaks in the paste become water entry points, and corrosion appears first at cable low points and under bands. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：之後安裝索夾（兩個半圓柱以螺栓夾緊，坡度越陡需要越多螺栓），掛上吊索，最後以纏絲機把鍍鋅軟鋼線（美國常用 No. 9 線）緊密纏繞在主纜外，並塗上防蝕膏與塗料，或改用彈性體包覆配合乾燥空氣。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cable bands are then installed, two half-cylinders bolted together, with more bolts on steeper slopes, the hangers are hung, and finally a wrapping machine winds soft galvanised wire (No. 9 wire in US practice) tightly around the cable over a corrosion-inhibiting paste and paint, or an elastomeric wrap is used with dry air.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「主纜擠壓只是為了外觀圓整，對耐久性影響不大。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Compaction is only to make the cable look round and hardly affects durability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"擠壓不足的區段在完工後仍持續壓密，索夾螺栓預力隨之流失，索夾可能下滑；纏絲間隙或防蝕膏不連續處成為水分入口，主纜低點與索夾下方最先出現腐蝕。","textEn":"Under-compacted sections keep consolidating after completion, so cable-band bolt preload is lost and bands may slip; gaps in wrapping or breaks in the paste become water entry points, and corrosion appears first at cable low points and under bands.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「主纜擠壓、纏絲與索夾安裝」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Compaction, wrapping and cable-band installation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["擠壓不足的區段在完工後仍持續壓密，索夾螺栓預力隨之流失，索夾可能下滑；纏絲間隙或防蝕膏不連續處成為水分入口，主纜低點與索夾下方最先出現腐蝕。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","儀器越精密，就不需要相對量測與交叉核對。"],"optionsEn":["Under-compacted sections keep consolidating after completion, so cable-band bolt preload is lost and bands may slip.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","With precise enough instruments, relative measurement and cross-checks are unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"擠壓不足的區段在完工後仍持續壓密，索夾螺栓預力隨之流失，索夾可能下滑；纏絲間隙或防蝕膏不連續處成為水分入口，主纜低點與索夾下方最先出現腐蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Under-compacted sections keep consolidating after completion, so cable-band bolt preload is lost and bands may slip; gaps in wrapping or breaks in the paste become water entry points, and corrosion appears first at cable low points and under bands. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b036-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「基準索股與相對垂度量測」與「鋼絲批次試驗與統計允收」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Reference strand and relative sag survey\" and \"Wire lot testing and statistical acceptance\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b036-v13-25","title":"基準索股與相對垂度量測：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Reference strand and relative sag survey: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「索股垂度量測精度」如何影響懸索橋主纜架設的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Strand sag survey accuracy” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-bridge main-cable erection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主纜每一股（或每一束）都要與基準索股的垂度一致，量測分兩層：基準索股以全站儀或精密水準做絕對量測，其餘索股則以安裝在跨中與邊跨的量規或雷射，量測與基準索股的相對高差。絕對量測的誤差主要來自儀器角度精度、距離、大氣折射與目標偏心；相對量測較不受大氣影響，但量規本身的定位與讀值方法必須統一。量測結果要與溫度紀錄一起判讀，並在調整後重新量測確認。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「索股垂度量測精度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Every strand or bundle must match the sag of the reference strand, and the survey works in two layers: the reference strand is measured absolutely by total station or precise levelling, while the others are measured relative to it with gauges or lasers mounted at mid-span and in the side spans. Absolute survey error comes mainly from instrument angular accuracy, distance, atmospheric refraction and target eccentricity; relative measurement is less affected by the atmosphere, but gauge positioning and reading method must be standardised. Results are interpreted with temperature records and re-measured after adjustment. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Strand sag survey accuracy” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：角度誤差造成的位置誤差 e ≈ D·θ。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Position error from angular error e ≈ D·θ.","failure":"常見誤解：「儀器越精密，就不需要相對量測與交叉核對。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With precise enough instruments, relative measurement and cross-checks are unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「索股垂度量測精度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Strand sag survey accuracy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-25-k1","title":"基準索股與相對垂度量測","titleEn":"Reference strand and relative sag survey","text":"主纜每一股（或每一束）都要與基準索股的垂度一致，量測分兩層：基準索股以全站儀或精密水準做絕對量測，其餘索股則以安裝在跨中與邊跨的量規或雷射，量測與基準索股的相對高差。絕對量測的誤差主要來自儀器角度精度、距離、大氣折射與目標偏心；相對量測較不受大氣影響，但量規本身的定位與讀值方法必須統一。","textEn":"Every strand or bundle must match the sag of the reference strand, and the survey works in two layers: the reference strand is measured absolutely by total station or precise levelling, while the others are measured relative to it with gauges or lasers mounted at mid-span and in the side spans. Absolute survey error comes mainly from instrument angular accuracy, distance, atmospheric refraction and target eccentricity; relative measurement is less affected by the atmosphere, but gauge positioning and reading method must be standardised.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：儀器越精密，就不需要相對量測與交叉核對。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With precise enough instruments, relative measurement and cross-checks are unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基準索股與相對垂度量測」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Reference strand and relative sag survey\" is correct?","options":["儀器越精密，就不需要相對量測與交叉核對。","主纜每一股（或每一束）都要與基準索股的垂度一致，量測分兩層：基準索股以全站儀或精密水準做絕對量測，其餘索股則以安裝在跨中與邊跨的量規或雷射，量測與基準索股的相對高差。","只要平均強度高於規格，整批鋼絲就合格。"],"optionsEn":["With precise enough instruments, relative measurement and cross-checks are unnecessary.","Every strand or bundle must match the sag of the reference strand, and the survey works in two layers: the reference strand is measured absolutely by total station or precise levelling, while the others are measured relative to it with gauges or lasers mounted at mid-span and in the side spans.","If the mean strength is above specification, the whole lot passes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"主纜每一股（或每一束）都要與基準索股的垂度一致，量測分兩層：基準索股以全站儀或精密水準做絕對量測，其餘索股則以安裝在跨中與邊跨的量規或雷射，量測與基準索股的相對高差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Every strand or bundle must match the sag of the reference strand, and the survey works in two layers: the reference strand is measured absolutely by total station or precise levelling, while the others are measured relative to it with gauges or lasers mounted at mid-span and in the side spans. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b036-v13-26","title":"基準索股與相對垂度量測：定量估算","titleEn":"Reference strand and relative sag survey: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「索股垂度量測精度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Strand sag survey accuracy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：角度誤差造成的位置誤差 e ≈ D·θ。全站儀角度精度 1″（4.85×10⁻⁶ rad）、視距 800 m：e ≈ 800×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 3.9 mm；若視距 1,600 m，e ≈ 7.8 mm。若索股相對高差允差為 ±10 mm，絕對量測在長視距下就會吃掉大部分允差，因此其他索股改用相對量測。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Position error from angular error e ≈ D·θ. With 1″ angular accuracy (4.85×10⁻⁶ rad) at 800 m, e ≈ 800×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 3.9 mm; at 1,600 m, e ≈ 7.8 mm. With a ±10 mm tolerance on relative strand level, absolute survey over long sights consumes most of the tolerance, which is why the other strands are measured relatively. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測前以已知點校核儀器與量規，量測時記錄氣溫、索股溫度、風速與時間，同一點由兩組人員獨立讀值；每股調整後的相對高差與基準索股的絕對量測定期交叉核對，發現系統偏差時追查量規或基準點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check instruments and gauges against known points before surveying; during the survey log air and strand temperature, wind and time, with two crews reading the same point independently; periodically cross-check adjusted relative levels against absolute surveys of the reference strand and trace gauges or benchmarks when a systematic offset appears.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"角度誤差造成的位置誤差 e ≈ D·θ。全站儀角度精度 1″（4.85×10⁻⁶ rad）、視距 800 m：e ≈ 800×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 3.9 mm；若視距 1,600 m，e ≈ 7.8 mm。若索股相對高差允差為 ±10 mm，絕對量測在長視距下就會吃掉大部分允差，因此其他索股改用相對量測。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Position error from angular error e ≈ D·θ. With 1″ angular accuracy (4.85×10⁻⁶ rad) at 800 m, e ≈ 800×4.85×10⁻⁶ ≈ 3.9 mm; at 1,600 m, e ≈ 7.8 mm. With a ±10 mm tolerance on relative strand level, absolute survey over long sights consumes most of the tolerance, which is why the other strands are measured relatively. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基準索股與相對垂度量測」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Reference strand and relative sag survey\", which statement holds?","options":["主纜強度在完工時就確定，之後只需目視檢查外觀。","主纜在任何階段都是拋物線，差別可以忽略。","角度誤差造成的位置誤差 e ≈ D·θ。"],"optionsEn":["Cable strength is fixed at completion, so only visual checks of the outside are needed afterwards.","The cable is a parabola at every stage, and the difference is negligible.","Position error from angular error e ≈ D·θ."],"answer":2,"explanation":"角度誤差造成的位置誤差 e ≈ D·θ。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Position error from angular error e ≈ D·θ. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b036-v13-27","title":"基準索股與相對垂度量測：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Reference strand and relative sag survey: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「索股垂度量測精度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Strand sag survey accuracy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測前以已知點校核儀器與量規，量測時記錄氣溫、索股溫度、風速與時間，同一點由兩組人員獨立讀值；每股調整後的相對高差與基準索股的絕對量測定期交叉核對，發現系統偏差時追查量規或基準點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check instruments and gauges against known points before surveying; during the survey log air and strand temperature, wind and time, with two crews reading the same point independently; periodically cross-check adjusted relative levels against absolute surveys of the reference strand and trace gauges or benchmarks when a systematic offset appears. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：量測程序書應明訂儀器精度、量測時段、兩組獨立讀值、允差與交叉核對頻率；任何連續數股同向偏差都應觸發停工檢查，由測量主管與設計代表共同判定後才繼續。","observationEn":"Site practice: The survey procedure should define instrument accuracy, measuring windows, two independent readings, tolerances and cross-check frequency; any run of strands deviating the same way should trigger a stop, resumed only after the survey lead and the designer's representative agree.","failure":"注意干擾：若基準索股量測含系統誤差，之後所有索股都會跟著錯，最後整條主纜垂度偏離設計；相對量規若在多股之後鬆動未被發現，造成一連串索股同向偏差，擠壓成纜後部分鋼絲受力過大。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A systematic error in the reference-strand survey carries into every strand that follows, leaving the whole cable off design sag; a relative gauge that loosens unnoticed after several strands produces a run of strands offset the same way, overloading some wires once compacted. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測前以已知點校核儀器與量規，量測時記錄氣溫、索股溫度、風速與時間，同一點由兩組人員獨立讀值；每股調整後的相對高差與基準索股的絕對量測定期交叉核對，發現系統偏差時追查量規或基準點。","textEn":"Check instruments and gauges against known points before surveying; during the survey log air and strand temperature, wind and time, with two crews reading the same point independently; periodically cross-check adjusted relative levels against absolute surveys of the reference strand and trace gauges or benchmarks when a systematic offset appears.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"量測程序書應明訂儀器精度、量測時段、兩組獨立讀值、允差與交叉核對頻率；任何連續數股同向偏差都應觸發停工檢查，由測量主管與設計代表共同判定後才繼續。","textEn":"The survey procedure should define instrument accuracy, measuring windows, two independent readings, tolerances and cross-check frequency; any run of strands deviating the same way should trigger a stop, resumed only after the survey lead and the designer's representative agree.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基準索股與相對垂度量測」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Reference strand and relative sag survey\"?","options":["量測前以已知點校核儀器與量規，量測時記錄氣溫、索股溫度、風速與時間，同一點由兩組人員獨立讀值。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","鋼絲只承受軸向拉力，索鞍形狀不影響應力。"],"optionsEn":["Check instruments and gauges against known points before surveying.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Cable wires carry only axial tension, so saddle shape does not affect stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測前以已知點校核儀器與量規，量測時記錄氣溫、索股溫度、風速與時間，同一點由兩組人員獨立讀值；每股調整後的相對高差與基準索股的絕對量測定期交叉核對，發現系統偏差時追查量規或基準點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check instruments and gauges against known points before surveying; during the survey log air and strand temperature, wind and time, with two crews reading the same point independently; periodically cross-check adjusted relative levels against absolute surveys of the reference strand and trace gauges or benchmarks when a systematic offset appears. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b036-v13-28","title":"基準索股與相對垂度量測：失效診斷","titleEn":"Reference strand and relative sag survey: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「索股垂度量測精度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Strand sag survey accuracy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若基準索股量測含系統誤差，之後所有索股都會跟著錯，最後整條主纜垂度偏離設計；相對量規若在多股之後鬆動未被發現，造成一連串索股同向偏差，擠壓成纜後部分鋼絲受力過大。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A systematic error in the reference-strand survey carries into every strand that follows, leaving the whole cable off design sag; a relative gauge that loosens unnoticed after several strands produces a run of strands offset the same way, overloading some wires once compacted. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：量測結果要與溫度紀錄一起判讀，並在調整後重新量測確認。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Results are interpreted with temperature records and re-measured after adjustment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「儀器越精密，就不需要相對量測與交叉核對。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With precise enough instruments, relative measurement and cross-checks are unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若基準索股量測含系統誤差，之後所有索股都會跟著錯，最後整條主纜垂度偏離設計；相對量規若在多股之後鬆動未被發現，造成一連串索股同向偏差，擠壓成纜後部分鋼絲受力過大。","textEn":"A systematic error in the reference-strand survey carries into every strand that follows, leaving the whole cable off design sag; a relative gauge that loosens unnoticed after several strands produces a run of strands offset the same way, overloading some wires once compacted.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基準索股與相對垂度量測」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Reference strand and relative sag survey\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若基準索股量測含系統誤差，之後所有索股都會跟著錯，最後整條主纜垂度偏離設計。","只要平均強度高於規格，整批鋼絲就合格。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A systematic error in the reference-strand survey carries into every strand that follows, leaving the whole cable off design sag.","If the mean strength is above specification, the whole lot passes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若基準索股量測含系統誤差，之後所有索股都會跟著錯，最後整條主纜垂度偏離設計；相對量規若在多股之後鬆動未被發現，造成一連串索股同向偏差，擠壓成纜後部分鋼絲受力過大。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A systematic error in the reference-strand survey carries into every strand that follows, leaving the whole cable off design sag; a relative gauge that loosens unnoticed after several strands produces a run of strands offset the same way, overloading some wires once compacted. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b036-v13-29","title":"鋼絲批次試驗與統計允收：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Wire lot testing and statistical acceptance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「鋼絲批次允收」如何影響懸索橋主纜架設的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wire lot acceptance” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-bridge main-cable erection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主纜由數萬根鋼絲組成，設計使用的是規格的最低強度或特徵值，而不是平均值；鋼絲強度呈統計分布，同一批次內也有差異。因此允收不能只看平均值，必須估計低分位值是否高於規格，並同時檢查伸長率、扭轉次數等延性指標與鍍層。製造過程任一環節（線材成分、熱處理、拉拔、鍍鋅）改變，都可能讓分布偏移，所以批次劃分與追溯同樣重要。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鋼絲批次允收」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A main cable contains tens of thousands of wires, and design uses the specified minimum or characteristic strength rather than the mean; wire strength follows a statistical distribution and varies within a lot. Acceptance therefore cannot rely on the mean alone: the lower fractile must be shown to exceed the specification, while ductility indicators such as elongation and torsion turns and the coating are checked too. A change in any manufacturing step, whether rod chemistry, heat treatment, drawing or galvanising, can shift the distribution, so lot definition and traceability matter as much. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Wire lot acceptance” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以常態分布估算 5% 分位值 f_k = f_m − 1.645·s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Estimate the 5% fractile from a normal distribution f_k = f_m − 1.645·s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要平均強度高於規格，整批鋼絲就合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the mean strength is above specification, the whole lot passes.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鋼絲批次允收」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Wire lot acceptance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-29-k1","title":"鋼絲批次試驗與統計允收","titleEn":"Wire lot testing and statistical acceptance","text":"主纜由數萬根鋼絲組成，設計使用的是規格的最低強度或特徵值，而不是平均值；鋼絲強度呈統計分布，同一批次內也有差異。因此允收不能只看平均值，必須估計低分位值是否高於規格，並同時檢查伸長率、扭轉次數等延性指標與鍍層。","textEn":"A main cable contains tens of thousands of wires, and design uses the specified minimum or characteristic strength rather than the mean; wire strength follows a statistical distribution and varies within a lot. Acceptance therefore cannot rely on the mean alone: the lower fractile must be shown to exceed the specification, while ductility indicators such as elongation and torsion turns and the coating are checked too.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要平均強度高於規格，整批鋼絲就合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the mean strength is above specification, the whole lot passes. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼絲批次試驗與統計允收」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wire lot testing and statistical acceptance\" is correct?","options":["只要平均強度高於規格，整批鋼絲就合格。","主纜外觀完好、塗裝沒有剝落，內部鋼絲就一定沒有腐蝕。","主纜由數萬根鋼絲組成，設計使用的是規格的最低強度或特徵值，而不是平均值；鋼絲強度呈統計分布，同一批次內也有差異。"],"optionsEn":["If the mean strength is above specification, the whole lot passes.","If the cable looks sound and its paint is intact, the wires inside cannot be corroded.","A main cable contains tens of thousands of wires, and design uses the specified minimum or characteristic strength rather than the mean."],"answer":2,"explanation":"主纜由數萬根鋼絲組成，設計使用的是規格的最低強度或特徵值，而不是平均值；鋼絲強度呈統計分布，同一批次內也有差異。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A main cable contains tens of thousands of wires, and design uses the specified minimum or characteristic strength rather than the mean; wire strength follows a statistical distribution and varies within a lot. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b036-v13-30","title":"鋼絲批次試驗與統計允收：定量估算","titleEn":"Wire lot testing and statistical acceptance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼絲批次允收」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wire lot acceptance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以常態分布估算 5% 分位值 f_k = f_m − 1.645·s。若某批平均強度 f_m = 1,860 N/mm²、標準差 s = 30 N/mm²：f_k = 1,860 − 1.645×30 ≈ 1,811 N/mm²，高於 1,770 N/mm² 的規格值；若 s 增為 55 N/mm²，f_k ≈ 1,770 N/mm²，剛好落在門檻。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Estimate the 5% fractile from a normal distribution f_k = f_m − 1.645·s. For a lot with mean f_m = 1,860 N/mm² and standard deviation s = 30 N/mm²: f_k = 1,860 − 1.645×30 ≈ 1,811 N/mm², above a 1,770 N/mm² specification; if s grows to 55 N/mm², f_k ≈ 1,770 N/mm², right at the threshold. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：依規格的抽樣頻率從每捲或每批取樣，做拉伸、扭轉、捲繞與鍍層試驗，計算平均、標準差與低分位值；趨勢圖顯示批間偏移時追查製程紀錄，並由第三方見證部分試驗，結果連同捲號納入追溯資料庫。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample each coil or lot at the specified frequency for tensile, torsion, wrapping and coating tests, computing mean, standard deviation and lower fractile; when trend charts show drift between lots, trace process records, have a third party witness part of the testing, and store results with coil numbers in the traceability database.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以常態分布估算 5% 分位值 f_k = f_m − 1.645·s。若某批平均強度 f_m = 1,860 N/mm²、標準差 s = 30 N/mm²：f_k = 1,860 − 1.645×30 ≈ 1,811 N/mm²，高於 1,770 N/mm² 的規格值；若 s 增為 55 N/mm²，f_k ≈ 1,770 N/mm²，剛好落在門檻。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Estimate the 5% fractile from a normal distribution f_k = f_m − 1.645·s. For a lot with mean f_m = 1,860 N/mm² and standard deviation s = 30 N/mm²: f_k = 1,860 − 1.645×30 ≈ 1,811 N/mm², above a 1,770 N/mm² specification; if s grows to 55 N/mm², f_k ≈ 1,770 N/mm², right at the threshold. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼絲批次試驗與統計允收」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wire lot testing and statistical acceptance\", which statement holds?","options":["以常態分布估算 5% 分位值 f_k = f_m − 1.645·s。","預製索股一定比空中紡線先進，任何橋都應該使用。","鍍鋅只是外觀處理，對主纜壽命影響不大。"],"optionsEn":["Estimate the 5% fractile from a normal distribution f_k = f_m − 1.645·s.","Prefabricated strands are always more advanced and should be used on every bridge.","Galvanising is cosmetic and hardly affects cable life."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以常態分布估算 5% 分位值 f_k = f_m − 1.645·s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Estimate the 5% fractile from a normal distribution f_k = f_m − 1.645·s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b036-v13-31","title":"鋼絲批次試驗與統計允收：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wire lot testing and statistical acceptance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼絲批次允收」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wire lot acceptance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"依規格的抽樣頻率從每捲或每批取樣，做拉伸、扭轉、捲繞與鍍層試驗，計算平均、標準差與低分位值；趨勢圖顯示批間偏移時追查製程紀錄，並由第三方見證部分試驗，結果連同捲號納入追溯資料庫。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample each coil or lot at the specified frequency for tensile, torsion, wrapping and coating tests, computing mean, standard deviation and lower fractile; when trend charts show drift between lots, trace process records, have a third party witness part of the testing, and store results with coil numbers in the traceability database. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：採購規範應明訂批次定義、抽樣頻率、統計允收準則與不合格批的處置（隔離、加倍抽樣或退貨），並要求製造商提交製程能力資料；允收紀錄須保存到橋梁使用年限結束。","observationEn":"Site practice: The procurement specification should define lots, sampling frequency, statistical acceptance criteria and disposal of failed lots (quarantine, double sampling or rejection), and require process-capability data from the maker; acceptance records must be kept for the bridge's whole service life.","failure":"注意干擾：只檢查平均值的允收方式，可能放行標準差過大的批次，使一部分鋼絲實際強度低於規格；延性不合格的鋼絲在架設時看不出問題，卻可能在索鞍、索夾的局部彎曲處提早斷裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Accepting on the mean alone can pass lots with too much scatter, leaving some wires below specification; wire with inadequate ductility looks fine during erection but may break early where it bends locally at saddles and bands. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依規格的抽樣頻率從每捲或每批取樣，做拉伸、扭轉、捲繞與鍍層試驗，計算平均、標準差與低分位值；趨勢圖顯示批間偏移時追查製程紀錄，並由第三方見證部分試驗，結果連同捲號納入追溯資料庫。","textEn":"Sample each coil or lot at the specified frequency for tensile, torsion, wrapping and coating tests, computing mean, standard deviation and lower fractile; when trend charts show drift between lots, trace process records, have a third party witness part of the testing, and store results with coil numbers in the traceability database.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"採購規範應明訂批次定義、抽樣頻率、統計允收準則與不合格批的處置（隔離、加倍抽樣或退貨），並要求製造商提交製程能力資料；允收紀錄須保存到橋梁使用年限結束。","textEn":"The procurement specification should define lots, sampling frequency, statistical acceptance criteria and disposal of failed lots (quarantine, double sampling or rejection), and require process-capability data from the maker; acceptance records must be kept for the bridge's whole service life.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼絲批次試驗與統計允收」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wire lot testing and statistical acceptance\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","依規格的抽樣頻率從每捲或每批取樣，做拉伸、扭轉、捲繞與鍍層試驗，計算平均、標準差與低分位值。","貓道只是臨時走道，可以用一般鷹架的標準設計。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Sample each coil or lot at the specified frequency for tensile, torsion, wrapping and coating tests, computing mean, standard deviation and lower fractile.","A catwalk is only a temporary walkway and can be designed like ordinary scaffolding."],"answer":1,"explanation":"依規格的抽樣頻率從每捲或每批取樣，做拉伸、扭轉、捲繞與鍍層試驗，計算平均、標準差與低分位值；趨勢圖顯示批間偏移時追查製程紀錄，並由第三方見證部分試驗，結果連同捲號納入追溯資料庫。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample each coil or lot at the specified frequency for tensile, torsion, wrapping and coating tests, computing mean, standard deviation and lower fractile; when trend charts show drift between lots, trace process records, have a third party witness part of the testing, and store results with coil numbers in the traceability database. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b036-v13-32","title":"鋼絲批次試驗與統計允收：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wire lot testing and statistical acceptance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼絲批次允收」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wire lot acceptance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只檢查平均值的允收方式，可能放行標準差過大的批次，使一部分鋼絲實際強度低於規格；延性不合格的鋼絲在架設時看不出問題，卻可能在索鞍、索夾的局部彎曲處提早斷裂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Accepting on the mean alone can pass lots with too much scatter, leaving some wires below specification; wire with inadequate ductility looks fine during erection but may break early where it bends locally at saddles and bands. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：製造過程任一環節（線材成分、熱處理、拉拔、鍍鋅）改變，都可能讓分布偏移，所以批次劃分與追溯同樣重要。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A change in any manufacturing step, whether rod chemistry, heat treatment, drawing or galvanising, can shift the distribution, so lot definition and traceability matter as much.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要平均強度高於規格，整批鋼絲就合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the mean strength is above specification, the whole lot passes.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只檢查平均值的允收方式，可能放行標準差過大的批次，使一部分鋼絲實際強度低於規格；延性不合格的鋼絲在架設時看不出問題，卻可能在索鞍、索夾的局部彎曲處提早斷裂。","textEn":"Accepting on the mean alone can pass lots with too much scatter, leaving some wires below specification; wire with inadequate ductility looks fine during erection but may break early where it bends locally at saddles and bands.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼絲批次試驗與統計允收」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wire lot testing and statistical acceptance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","主纜外觀完好、塗裝沒有剝落，內部鋼絲就一定沒有腐蝕。","只檢查平均值的允收方式，可能放行標準差過大的批次，使一部分鋼絲實際強度低於規格；延性不合格的鋼絲在架設時看不出問題，卻可能在索鞍、索夾的局部彎曲處提早斷裂。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","If the cable looks sound and its paint is intact, the wires inside cannot be corroded.","Accepting on the mean alone can pass lots with too much scatter, leaving some wires below specification."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只檢查平均值的允收方式，可能放行標準差過大的批次，使一部分鋼絲實際強度低於規格；延性不合格的鋼絲在架設時看不出問題，卻可能在索鞍、索夾的局部彎曲處提早斷裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Accepting on the mean alone can pass lots with too much scatter, leaving some wires below specification; wire with inadequate ductility looks fine during erection but may break early where it bends locally at saddles and bands. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b036-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「主纜內部檢查與腐蝕分級」與「主纜剩餘強度評估與交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Internal cable inspection and corrosion staging\" and \"Remaining-strength evaluation and handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b036-v13-33","title":"主纜內部檢查與腐蝕分級：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Internal cable inspection and corrosion staging: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「楔形開纜檢查」如何影響懸索橋主纜架設的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wedge-opening inspection” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-bridge main-cable erection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主纜外表的纏絲與塗裝看不出內部狀況，唯一直接的方法是拆開包覆、以楔子撐開鋼絲檢查。美國聯邦公路總署的入門手冊建議首次內部檢查每條主纜至少三處，每處在周圍四個位置打入楔子；若腐蝕超過第 2 級，開口擴大到整個格間並使用八條楔線。腐蝕分為四級：第 1 級鋼絲表面有白點，第 2 級整個表面白色鋅氧化，第 3 級部分出現褐色鏽點，第 4 級褐色鏽點覆蓋 3 至 6 in 長度內超過 30% 的表面。實驗顯示約 60% 的第 4 級鋼絲可能含有裂紋。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「楔形開纜檢查」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wrapping and paint hide the inside of a cable, and the only direct method is to remove the covering and drive wedges to spread the wires. The US Federal Highway Administration primer recommends that a first internal inspection open at least three locations per cable, with wedges at four points around the circumference; if corrosion exceeds Stage 2, the opening extends to a full panel with eight wedge lines. Corrosion has four stages: Stage 1 white spots on the wire surface, Stage 2 white zinc oxide over the whole surface, Stage 3 some brown rust spots, and Stage 4 brown spots covering more than 30% of a 3 to 6 in length of wire. Laboratory tests showed that about 60% of Stage 4 wires may contain cracks. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Wedge-opening inspection” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：估算楔線可見鋼絲的比例。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Estimate the share of wires seen along wedge lines.","failure":"常見誤解：「主纜外觀完好、塗裝沒有剝落，內部鋼絲就一定沒有腐蝕。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the cable looks sound and its paint is intact, the wires inside cannot be corroded.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「楔形開纜檢查」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Wedge-opening inspection”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-33-k1","title":"主纜內部檢查與腐蝕分級","titleEn":"Internal cable inspection and corrosion staging","text":"主纜外表的纏絲與塗裝看不出內部狀況，唯一直接的方法是拆開包覆、以楔子撐開鋼絲檢查。美國聯邦公路總署的入門手冊建議首次內部檢查每條主纜至少三處，每處在周圍四個位置打入楔子；若腐蝕超過第 2 級，開口擴大到整個格間並使用八條楔線。","textEn":"Wrapping and paint hide the inside of a cable, and the only direct method is to remove the covering and drive wedges to spread the wires. The US Federal Highway Administration primer recommends that a first internal inspection open at least three locations per cable, with wedges at four points around the circumference; if corrosion exceeds Stage 2, the opening extends to a full panel with eight wedge lines.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：主纜外觀完好、塗裝沒有剝落，內部鋼絲就一定沒有腐蝕。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the cable looks sound and its paint is intact, the wires inside cannot be corroded. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「主纜內部檢查與腐蝕分級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Internal cable inspection and corrosion staging\" is correct?","options":["主纜外表的纏絲與塗裝看不出內部狀況，唯一直接的方法是拆開包覆、以楔子撐開鋼絲檢查。","主纜外觀完好、塗裝沒有剝落，內部鋼絲就一定沒有腐蝕。","主纜強度在完工時就確定，之後只需目視檢查外觀。"],"optionsEn":["Wrapping and paint hide the inside of a cable, and the only direct method is to remove the covering and drive wedges to spread the wires.","If the cable looks sound and its paint is intact, the wires inside cannot be corroded.","Cable strength is fixed at completion, so only visual checks of the outside are needed afterwards."],"answer":0,"explanation":"主纜外表的纏絲與塗裝看不出內部狀況，唯一直接的方法是拆開包覆、以楔子撐開鋼絲檢查。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wrapping and paint hide the inside of a cable, and the only direct method is to remove the covering and drive wedges to spread the wires. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b036-v13-34","title":"主纜內部檢查與腐蝕分級：定量估算","titleEn":"Internal cable inspection and corrosion staging: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「楔形開纜檢查」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wedge-opening inspection” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：估算楔線可見鋼絲的比例。主纜半徑 0.4 m、鋼絲直徑 5.4 mm，徑向約 0.4/0.0054 ≈ 74 層；每條楔線兩側各見一根，約 148 根；8 條楔線約 1,185 根，佔 18,000 根的約 6.6%。這說明開纜檢查是抽樣，需要統計推估全斷面。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Estimate the share of wires seen along wedge lines. With a 0.4 m cable radius and 5.4 mm wire there are about 0.4/0.0054 ≈ 74 radial layers; each wedge line shows one wire on each side, about 148 wires; eight lines show about 1,185 wires, about 6.6% of 18,000. Cable openings are therefore a sample, and the whole section must be inferred statistically. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：開纜位置優先選在主纜低點、索夾附近與歷史漏水處；每條楔線逐層記錄腐蝕等級與斷絲，取出代表性鋼絲做拉伸與裂紋檢查；首次基準檢查建議在約 30 年時進行，若第 4 級鋼絲超過 10%，下次間隔縮短到 5 年。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Choose openings at cable low points, near cable bands and where leaks have been recorded; log corrosion stage and broken wires layer by layer along each wedge line and remove representative wires for tensile and crack tests; the baseline internal inspection is suggested at about 30 years, with the interval shortened to five years if more than 10% of wires are Stage 4.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"估算楔線可見鋼絲的比例。主纜半徑 0.4 m、鋼絲直徑 5.4 mm，徑向約 0.4/0.0054 ≈ 74 層；每條楔線兩側各見一根，約 148 根；8 條楔線約 1,185 根，佔 18,000 根的約 6.6%。這說明開纜檢查是抽樣，需要統計推估全斷面。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Estimate the share of wires seen along wedge lines. With a 0.4 m cable radius and 5.4 mm wire there are about 0.4/0.0054 ≈ 74 radial layers; each wedge line shows one wire on each side, about 148 wires; eight lines show about 1,185 wires, about 6.6% of 18,000. Cable openings are therefore a sample, and the whole section must be inferred statistically. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「主纜內部檢查與腐蝕分級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Internal cable inspection and corrosion staging\", which statement holds?","options":["主纜在任何階段都是拋物線，差別可以忽略。","估算楔線可見鋼絲的比例。","鋼絲只承受軸向拉力，索鞍形狀不影響應力。"],"optionsEn":["The cable is a parabola at every stage, and the difference is negligible.","Estimate the share of wires seen along wedge lines.","Cable wires carry only axial tension, so saddle shape does not affect stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"估算楔線可見鋼絲的比例。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Estimate the share of wires seen along wedge lines. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b036-v13-35","title":"主纜內部檢查與腐蝕分級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Internal cable inspection and corrosion staging: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「楔形開纜檢查」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wedge-opening inspection” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"開纜位置優先選在主纜低點、索夾附近與歷史漏水處；每條楔線逐層記錄腐蝕等級與斷絲，取出代表性鋼絲做拉伸與裂紋檢查；首次基準檢查建議在約 30 年時進行，若第 4 級鋼絲超過 10%，下次間隔縮短到 5 年。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Choose openings at cable low points, near cable bands and where leaks have been recorded; log corrosion stage and broken wires layer by layer along each wedge line and remove representative wires for tensile and crack tests; the baseline internal inspection is suggested at about 30 years, with the interval shortened to five years if more than 10% of wires are Stage 4. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：開纜檢查計畫應說明位置選擇理由、楔線數量、記錄格式、取樣鋼絲數與重新包覆的品質要求，並由具主纜檢查經驗的工程師主持；所有開口位置與結果須標示在主纜展開圖上供日後比較。","observationEn":"Site practice: The cable-opening plan should justify locations, wedge-line count, record format, number of sampled wires and rewrapping quality, led by an engineer experienced in cable inspection; mark every opening and its findings on a developed cable drawing for later comparison.","failure":"注意干擾：若只在容易到達的高處開纜，可能錯過積水最嚴重的低點；檢查後重新包覆不良，開口本身反而成為新的進水點；把第 4 級鋼絲當作完好鋼絲計算，會高估主纜強度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Opening only where access is easy can miss the wettest low points; poor rewrapping after inspection turns the opening into a new water entry; counting Stage 4 wires as sound overstates cable strength. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"開纜位置優先選在主纜低點、索夾附近與歷史漏水處；每條楔線逐層記錄腐蝕等級與斷絲，取出代表性鋼絲做拉伸與裂紋檢查；首次基準檢查建議在約 30 年時進行，若第 4 級鋼絲超過 10%，下次間隔縮短到 5 年。","textEn":"Choose openings at cable low points, near cable bands and where leaks have been recorded; log corrosion stage and broken wires layer by layer along each wedge line and remove representative wires for tensile and crack tests; the baseline internal inspection is suggested at about 30 years, with the interval shortened to five years if more than 10% of wires are Stage 4.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"開纜檢查計畫應說明位置選擇理由、楔線數量、記錄格式、取樣鋼絲數與重新包覆的品質要求，並由具主纜檢查經驗的工程師主持；所有開口位置與結果須標示在主纜展開圖上供日後比較。","textEn":"The cable-opening plan should justify locations, wedge-line count, record format, number of sampled wires and rewrapping quality, led by an engineer experienced in cable inspection; mark every opening and its findings on a developed cable drawing for later comparison.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「主纜內部檢查與腐蝕分級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Internal cable inspection and corrosion staging\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","主纜擠壓只是為了外觀圓整，對耐久性影響不大。","開纜位置優先選在主纜低點、索夾附近與歷史漏水處。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Compaction is only to make the cable look round and hardly affects durability.","Choose openings at cable low points, near cable bands and where leaks have been recorded."],"answer":2,"explanation":"開纜位置優先選在主纜低點、索夾附近與歷史漏水處；每條楔線逐層記錄腐蝕等級與斷絲，取出代表性鋼絲做拉伸與裂紋檢查；首次基準檢查建議在約 30 年時進行，若第 4 級鋼絲超過 10%，下次間隔縮短到 5 年。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Choose openings at cable low points, near cable bands and where leaks have been recorded; log corrosion stage and broken wires layer by layer along each wedge line and remove representative wires for tensile and crack tests; the baseline internal inspection is suggested at about 30 years, with the interval shortened to five years if more than 10% of wires are Stage 4. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b036-v13-36","title":"主纜內部檢查與腐蝕分級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Internal cable inspection and corrosion staging: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「楔形開纜檢查」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wedge-opening inspection” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只在容易到達的高處開纜，可能錯過積水最嚴重的低點；檢查後重新包覆不良，開口本身反而成為新的進水點；把第 4 級鋼絲當作完好鋼絲計算，會高估主纜強度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Opening only where access is easy can miss the wettest low points; poor rewrapping after inspection turns the opening into a new water entry; counting Stage 4 wires as sound overstates cable strength. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：實驗顯示約 60% 的第 4 級鋼絲可能含有裂紋。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Laboratory tests showed that about 60% of Stage 4 wires may contain cracks.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「主纜外觀完好、塗裝沒有剝落，內部鋼絲就一定沒有腐蝕。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the cable looks sound and its paint is intact, the wires inside cannot be corroded.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只在容易到達的高處開纜，可能錯過積水最嚴重的低點；檢查後重新包覆不良，開口本身反而成為新的進水點；把第 4 級鋼絲當作完好鋼絲計算，會高估主纜強度。","textEn":"Opening only where access is easy can miss the wettest low points; poor rewrapping after inspection turns the opening into a new water entry; counting Stage 4 wires as sound overstates cable strength.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「主纜內部檢查與腐蝕分級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Internal cable inspection and corrosion staging\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若只在容易到達的高處開纜，可能錯過積水最嚴重的低點；檢查後重新包覆不良，開口本身反而成為新的進水點；把第 4 級鋼絲當作完好鋼絲計算，會高估主纜強度。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","主纜強度在完工時就確定，之後只需目視檢查外觀。"],"optionsEn":["Opening only where access is easy can miss the wettest low points.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Cable strength is fixed at completion, so only visual checks of the outside are needed afterwards."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若只在容易到達的高處開纜，可能錯過積水最嚴重的低點；檢查後重新包覆不良，開口本身反而成為新的進水點；把第 4 級鋼絲當作完好鋼絲計算，會高估主纜強度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Opening only where access is easy can miss the wettest low points; poor rewrapping after inspection turns the opening into a new water entry; counting Stage 4 wires as sound overstates cable strength. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b036-v13-37","title":"主纜剩餘強度評估與交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Remaining-strength evaluation and handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「剩餘強度與聲學監測」如何影響懸索橋主纜架設的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Remaining strength and acoustic monitoring” governs force, deformation or durability in “Suspension-bridge main-cable erection”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主纜剩餘強度評估把開纜觀察、鋼絲試驗與統計模型結合起來。美國的 NCHRP 534 號報告提出三種模型：裂紋鋼絲不超過總數約 10% 時可用簡化模型，它在多數情況下低估強度，適合找出最不利格間；超過時改用脆性鋼絲模型；鋼絲強度變異異常時用有限延性模型。聯邦公路總署建議在發現第 3 級以上腐蝕時裝設聲學監測，在下次開纜前持續 12 至 18 個月；當第 4 級鋼絲超過 10% 或格間內出現斷絲時，強烈建議以聲學監測偵測斷絲。這些資料都必須在交接時從施工記錄開始累積。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「剩餘強度與聲學監測」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Remaining-strength evaluation combines cable observations, wire tests and statistical models. US NCHRP Report 534 offers three: a simplified model when cracked wires are no more than about 10% of the total, which usually underestimates strength and is useful for finding the worst panel; a brittle-wire model beyond that; and a limited-ductility model when wire strength varies unusually. The Federal Highway Administration recommends acoustic monitoring once Stage 3 or worse corrosion is found, running 12 to 18 months before the next opening, and strongly recommends it for detecting wire breaks when Stage 4 wires exceed 10% or broken wires appear in a panel. All these data must accumulate from the construction records handed over at completion. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Remaining strength and acoustic monitoring” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：簡化估算：18,000 根鋼絲中 2% 斷絲（360 根）、10% 為第 4 級（1,800 根），其中 60% 含裂紋（1,080 根）且假設僅剩 50% 強度。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Simplified estimate: of 18,000 wires, 2% are broken (360) and 10% are Stage 4 (1,800), of which 60% are cracked (1,080) and assumed to keep 50% strength.","failure":"常見誤解：「主纜強度在完工時就確定，之後只需目視檢查外觀。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cable strength is fixed at completion, so only visual checks of the outside are needed afterwards.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「剩餘強度與聲學監測」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Remaining strength and acoustic monitoring”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-37-k1","title":"主纜剩餘強度評估與交接","titleEn":"Remaining-strength evaluation and handover","text":"主纜剩餘強度評估把開纜觀察、鋼絲試驗與統計模型結合起來。美國的 NCHRP 534 號報告提出三種模型：裂紋鋼絲不超過總數約 10% 時可用簡化模型，它在多數情況下低估強度，適合找出最不利格間；超過時改用脆性鋼絲模型；鋼絲強度變異異常時用有限延性模型。","textEn":"Remaining-strength evaluation combines cable observations, wire tests and statistical models. US NCHRP Report 534 offers three: a simplified model when cracked wires are no more than about 10% of the total, which usually underestimates strength and is useful for finding the worst panel; a brittle-wire model beyond that; and a limited-ductility model when wire strength varies unusually.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：主纜強度在完工時就確定，之後只需目視檢查外觀。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cable strength is fixed at completion, so only visual checks of the outside are needed afterwards. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「主纜剩餘強度評估與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Remaining-strength evaluation and handover\" is correct?","options":["主纜強度在完工時就確定，之後只需目視檢查外觀。","主纜剩餘強度評估把開纜觀察、鋼絲試驗與統計模型結合起來。","預製索股一定比空中紡線先進，任何橋都應該使用。"],"optionsEn":["Cable strength is fixed at completion, so only visual checks of the outside are needed afterwards.","Remaining-strength evaluation combines cable observations, wire tests and statistical models.","Prefabricated strands are always more advanced and should be used on every bridge."],"answer":1,"explanation":"主纜剩餘強度評估把開纜觀察、鋼絲試驗與統計模型結合起來。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Remaining-strength evaluation combines cable observations, wire tests and statistical models. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b036-v13-38","title":"主纜剩餘強度評估與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Remaining-strength evaluation and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剩餘強度與聲學監測」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Remaining strength and acoustic monitoring” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：簡化估算：18,000 根鋼絲中 2% 斷絲（360 根）、10% 為第 4 級（1,800 根），其中 60% 含裂紋（1,080 根）且假設僅剩 50% 強度。有效鋼絲 = 18,000 − 360 − 1,080×0.5 = 17,100 根，強度剩 95%；原安全係數 2.5 降為約 2.375。若斷絲增為 5%，有效鋼絲 16,560 根，係數約 2.30。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Simplified estimate: of 18,000 wires, 2% are broken (360) and 10% are Stage 4 (1,800), of which 60% are cracked (1,080) and assumed to keep 50% strength. Effective wires = 18,000 − 360 − 1,080×0.5 = 17,100, or 95% of strength, so a 2.5 safety factor falls to about 2.375. If broken wires rise to 5%, effective wires are 16,560 and the factor is about 2.30. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以開纜位置的逐層紀錄與試驗結果建立各格間的強度估計，標出最不利格間；聲學監測系統需先做斷絲模擬試驗確認偵測率與定位精度，運轉期間把事件位置與時間標在主纜展開圖上，與下一次開纜結果對照。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build strength estimates for each panel from layer-by-layer opening records and test results, identifying the worst panel; validate an acoustic monitoring system with simulated wire breaks to confirm detection rate and location accuracy, then plot events by position and time on the developed cable drawing and compare with the next opening.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"簡化估算：18,000 根鋼絲中 2% 斷絲（360 根）、10% 為第 4 級（1,800 根），其中 60% 含裂紋（1,080 根）且假設僅剩 50% 強度。有效鋼絲 = 18,000 − 360 − 1,080×0.5 = 17,100 根，強度剩 95%；原安全係數 2.5 降為約 2.375。若斷絲增為 5%，有效鋼絲 16,560 根，係數約 2.30。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Simplified estimate: of 18,000 wires, 2% are broken (360) and 10% are Stage 4 (1,800), of which 60% are cracked (1,080) and assumed to keep 50% strength. Effective wires = 18,000 − 360 − 1,080×0.5 = 17,100, or 95% of strength, so a 2.5 safety factor falls to about 2.375. If broken wires rise to 5%, effective wires are 16,560 and the factor is about 2.30. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「主纜剩餘強度評估與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Remaining-strength evaluation and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["鍍鋅只是外觀處理，對主纜壽命影響不大。","貓道只是臨時走道，可以用一般鷹架的標準設計。","簡化估算：18,000 根鋼絲中 2% 斷絲（360 根）、10% 為第 4 級（1,800 根），其中 60% 含裂紋（1,080 根）且假設僅剩 50% 強度。"],"optionsEn":["Galvanising is cosmetic and hardly affects cable life.","A catwalk is only a temporary walkway and can be designed like ordinary scaffolding.","Simplified estimate: of 18,000 wires, 2% are broken (360) and 10% are Stage 4 (1,800), of which 60% are cracked (1,080) and assumed to keep 50% strength."],"answer":2,"explanation":"簡化估算：18,000 根鋼絲中 2% 斷絲（360 根）、10% 為第 4 級（1,800 根），其中 60% 含裂紋（1,080 根）且假設僅剩 50% 強度。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Simplified estimate: of 18,000 wires, 2% are broken (360) and 10% are Stage 4 (1,800), of which 60% are cracked (1,080) and assumed to keep 50% strength. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b036-v13-39","title":"主纜剩餘強度評估與交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Remaining-strength evaluation and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剩餘強度與聲學監測」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Remaining strength and acoustic monitoring” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以開纜位置的逐層紀錄與試驗結果建立各格間的強度估計，標出最不利格間；聲學監測系統需先做斷絲模擬試驗確認偵測率與定位精度，運轉期間把事件位置與時間標在主纜展開圖上，與下一次開纜結果對照。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build strength estimates for each panel from layer-by-layer opening records and test results, identifying the worst panel; validate an acoustic monitoring system with simulated wire breaks to confirm detection rate and location accuracy, then plot events by position and time on the developed cable drawing and compare with the next opening. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件應包含主纜展開圖、各束或各股的鋼絲數與批號、量測與允收紀錄、擠壓與纏絲紀錄、索夾螺栓張力，以及建議的首次開纜時間；營運單位據此建立主纜資料庫，每次檢查與監測都回寫更新。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover documents should contain the developed cable drawing, wire count and lot numbers per strand or bundle, survey and acceptance records, compaction and wrapping records, cable-band bolt tensions and the recommended time of the first opening; the operator builds a cable database from them and updates it after every inspection and monitoring campaign.","failure":"注意干擾：缺少施工時的鋼絲批次、空隙率與纏絲紀錄，評估者只能用保守假設，可能導致不必要的限載或過晚的介入；聲學事件若未與檢查結果比對，誤報與漏報都無法被修正。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without construction records of wire lots, void ratio and wrapping, evaluators must use conservative assumptions that can cause needless load limits or late intervention; acoustic events never compared with inspection results leave false alarms and missed breaks uncorrected. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以開纜位置的逐層紀錄與試驗結果建立各格間的強度估計，標出最不利格間；聲學監測系統需先做斷絲模擬試驗確認偵測率與定位精度，運轉期間把事件位置與時間標在主纜展開圖上，與下一次開纜結果對照。","textEn":"Build strength estimates for each panel from layer-by-layer opening records and test results, identifying the worst panel; validate an acoustic monitoring system with simulated wire breaks to confirm detection rate and location accuracy, then plot events by position and time on the developed cable drawing and compare with the next opening.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件應包含主纜展開圖、各束或各股的鋼絲數與批號、量測與允收紀錄、擠壓與纏絲紀錄、索夾螺栓張力，以及建議的首次開纜時間；營運單位據此建立主纜資料庫，每次檢查與監測都回寫更新。","textEn":"Handover documents should contain the developed cable drawing, wire count and lot numbers per strand or bundle, survey and acceptance records, compaction and wrapping records, cable-band bolt tensions and the recommended time of the first opening; the operator builds a cable database from them and updates it after every inspection and monitoring campaign.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「主纜剩餘強度評估與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Remaining-strength evaluation and handover\"?","options":["以開纜位置的逐層紀錄與試驗結果建立各格間的強度估計，標出最不利格間。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","儀器越精密，就不需要相對量測與交叉核對。"],"optionsEn":["Build strength estimates for each panel from layer-by-layer opening records and test results, identifying the worst panel.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","With precise enough instruments, relative measurement and cross-checks are unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以開纜位置的逐層紀錄與試驗結果建立各格間的強度估計，標出最不利格間；聲學監測系統需先做斷絲模擬試驗確認偵測率與定位精度，運轉期間把事件位置與時間標在主纜展開圖上，與下一次開纜結果對照。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build strength estimates for each panel from layer-by-layer opening records and test results, identifying the worst panel; validate an acoustic monitoring system with simulated wire breaks to confirm detection rate and location accuracy, then plot events by position and time on the developed cable drawing and compare with the next opening. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b036-v13-40","title":"主纜剩餘強度評估與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Remaining-strength evaluation and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"prerequisiteIds":["b036-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剩餘強度與聲學監測」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Remaining strength and acoustic monitoring” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"缺少施工時的鋼絲批次、空隙率與纏絲紀錄，評估者只能用保守假設，可能導致不必要的限載或過晚的介入；聲學事件若未與檢查結果比對，誤報與漏報都無法被修正。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without construction records of wire lots, void ratio and wrapping, evaluators must use conservative assumptions that can cause needless load limits or late intervention; acoustic events never compared with inspection results leave false alarms and missed breaks uncorrected. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這些資料都必須在交接時從施工記錄開始累積。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: All these data must accumulate from the construction records handed over at completion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「主纜強度在完工時就確定，之後只需目視檢查外觀。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cable strength is fixed at completion, so only visual checks of the outside are needed afterwards.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b036-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"缺少施工時的鋼絲批次、空隙率與纏絲紀錄，評估者只能用保守假設，可能導致不必要的限載或過晚的介入；聲學事件若未與檢查結果比對，誤報與漏報都無法被修正。","textEn":"Without construction records of wire lots, void ratio and wrapping, evaluators must use conservative assumptions that can cause needless load limits or late intervention; acoustic events never compared with inspection results leave false alarms and missed breaks uncorrected.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]},{"id":"b036-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「主纜剩餘強度評估與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Remaining-strength evaluation and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","缺少施工時的鋼絲批次、空隙率與纏絲紀錄，評估者只能用保守假設，可能導致不必要的限載或過晚的介入；聲學事件若未與檢查結果比對，誤報與漏報都無法被修正。","預製索股一定比空中紡線先進，任何橋都應該使用。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Without construction records of wire lots, void ratio and wrapping, evaluators must use conservative assumptions that can cause needless load limits or late intervention.","Prefabricated strands are always more advanced and should be used on every bridge."],"answer":1,"explanation":"缺少施工時的鋼絲批次、空隙率與纏絲紀錄，評估者只能用保守假設，可能導致不必要的限載或過晚的介入；聲學事件若未與檢查結果比對，誤報與漏報都無法被修正。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without construction records of wire lots, void ratio and wrapping, evaluators must use conservative assumptions that can cause needless load limits or late intervention; acoustic events never compared with inspection results leave false alarms and missed breaks uncorrected. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-fhwa-cable-primer","v7-golden-stats","v13s-jb-seto-ohashi-cable","v13s-nippon-steel-pws-wire","v13s-sundogbaelt-storebaelt"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
